public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1f80e71d6dff58e117a7422105f9a7cfde560e80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:33:56Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:33:56Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"docs: sync the temperature_sender snippet with the example\n\nThe concepts page quotes temperature_sender.cpp as AnalogInput ->\nAnalogVoltage -> VoltageDividerR2. The example stopped using either\nclass: it reads the pin through a RepeatSensor over\nanalogReadMilliVolts() and feeds volts straight into VoltageDividerR2.\n\nThe stale snippet is also a chain nobody should copy. AnalogVoltage\ndivides by kMaxAnalogOutput (4096) while AnalogInput''s default\noutput_scale is 1024, so the two defaults disagree by a factor of four\nand the voltage handed to VoltageDividerR2 is four times too low.\n\nQuote what the example actually does instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d9bc511f37b64192e671899fa70ba477d0ad63e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/4d9bc511f37b64192e671899fa70ba477d0ad63e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/1f80e71d6dff58e117a7422105f9a7cfde560e80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/1f80e71d6dff58e117a7422105f9a7cfde560e80","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDFmODBlNzFkNmRmZjU4ZTExN2E3NDIyMTA1ZjlhN2NmZGU1NjBlODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94","sha":"71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94"}],"sha":"1f80e71d6dff58e117a7422105f9a7cfde560e80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1f80e71d6dff58e117a7422105f9a7cfde560e80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:29:53Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:30:39Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"docs: clarify that tank level examples use AnalogInput readings\n\nThe examples quote 1023, 826, 43 and 991 without saying where those\nnumbers come from, which reads as raw ADC counts. They are values\nreported by AnalogInput at its default output_scale of 1024, which is\nwhat makes the 1024 / range formulas correct - a reader who substitutes\nraw counts from an ESP32 gets a scale that is off by four.\n\nState that once up front, correct the full-scale figure from the\nESP8266-era 1023 to 1024, and stop calling the reported value \"raw\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5cf42285982f89087374a0e7400ed767b8535c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/d5cf42285982f89087374a0e7400ed767b8535c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDcxZjBlMmIwNzlhYTk1YzlkZTc0YzgxZTllMGE4NDhkOTk2MmZmOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b","sha":"1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b"}],"sha":"71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/71f0e2b079aa95c9de74c81e9e0a848d9962ff94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:29:53Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:29:53Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"fix(sensors): reject invalid ESP32AnalogReader reference voltages\n\nmax_voltage is the divisor in read(). A zero, negative or non-finite\nvalue makes read() return infinity, NaN or a negative fraction, which\npropagates silently through AnalogInput into the Signal K output.\n\nLog the bad value and fall back to the 3300 mV default instead, and\nname that default kDefaultMaxVoltage so it is not repeated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68af958fdee60275d0fba64a0ded93a9cbb13a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/68af958fdee60275d0fba64a0ded93a9cbb13a4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDEzNDU1MDM4MTNhZjI3MWRkNDNlMzFjNjY5NzE3ODBjYzgzNzk3MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc","sha":"3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc"}],"sha":"1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1345503813af271dd43e31c66971780cc837972b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:58:51Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:58:51Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"docs: correct AnalogInput documentation and add migration notes\n\nThe tank level tutorial described output_scale as mapping the raw\nanalogRead() value onto a 0..output_scale-1 range, and suggested raising\nit to 4096 for \"full precision\". Neither is true of a normalized\ncalibrated voltage: output_scale chooses the units of the output, not\nits precision.\n\nThe concepts guide showed constructor calls predating the v2 signature.\nnew AnalogInput(250, \"/analogInput\") has not compiled since config_path\nstopped being the second parameter, and new AnalogInput(250) sets pin\n250 rather than a 250 ms read delay.\n\nAdd a migration section covering both fixes and the undeprecation,\nincluding a warning to undo the output_scale workaround from #812, which\nnow makes readings about 4096x too small in the other direction.\n\nCHANGELOG.md has not been touched since 2020, so these notes go in the\nmigration guide, alongside the existing \"Transport-agnostic networking\n(v3 minor update)\" section.\n\nRefs: #812","tree":{"sha":"2b54cecc08e8cd6725ad97694ffd2fa25ce42e93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/2b54cecc08e8cd6725ad97694ffd2fa25ce42e93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDNjM2JlY2ViMjMxN2MyOTc4MjQ5YzI4OTllMzBhNGE1OTYwOTgyZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe","sha":"1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe"}],"sha":"3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/3c3beceb2317c2978249c2899e30a4a5960982fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:58:28Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:58:28Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"fix(sensors): apply persisted read delay and undeprecate AnalogInput\n\nThe constructor parameters pin, read_delay and output_scale shared the\nnames of the members they initialize, so within the constructor body the\nparameters shadowed the members. load() runs there and replaces the\nread_delay member with the value persisted in the file system, but the\nonRepeat() call that follows read the parameter instead. A Read delay\nset in the web UI was therefore saved, reloaded, and then ignored --\neven across a restart, despite ConfigRequiresRestart() returning true.\nThe setting has never had any effect.\n\nRename the members to pin_, read_delay_ and output_scale_, following the\nconvention applied across the codebase in 7c241c9ba, which this class\nwas missed by. That removes the shadowing at its source instead of\nqualifying the single call site.\n\nWith readings correct again, drop the [[deprecated]] attribute. The\nclass was deprecated once it stopped calibrating and became a thin\nwrapper over analogRead(). Now that it reads a calibrated voltage it\noffers something RepeatSensor cannot: RepeatSensor hardcodes an empty\nconfig_path, so it can never expose its interval in the web UI.\n\nRemoving the attribute also removes the need for the\n-Wdeprecated-declarations suppressions around ConfigSchema() and\nConfigRequiresRestart(). Those overloads have to name the class, so the\nattribute made the library warn in every translation unit that included\nthe header, including ones that never touch AnalogInput.\n\nRefs: #812, #826","tree":{"sha":"2ce976f47c41b512496fd6634e556e97e4a108f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/2ce976f47c41b512496fd6634e556e97e4a108f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDE1MDAwMzlmNTAyMTYyYjM2Njc1N2QwZDg1MTk5MzMwNTVmMzNlZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/375d0db35a02821f5313d251bc23f79bfb6224b5","sha":"375d0db35a02821f5313d251bc23f79bfb6224b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/375d0db35a02821f5313d251bc23f79bfb6224b5"}],"sha":"1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/1500039f502162b366757d0d8519933055f33efe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/375d0db35a02821f5313d251bc23f79bfb6224b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:57:16Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:57:16Z","email":"ke.gustafsson@gmail.com","name":"Karl-Erik Gustafsson"},"message":"fix(sensors): restore calibrated, normalized analog readings\n\nAnalogReader::read() has returned the raw analogRead() count ever since\nfa5070d10 removed the ESP-IDF ADC calibration layer. AnalogInput\nmultiplies that result by output_scale on the assumption that it is a\n0..1 fraction, so with the default output_scale of 1024 the emitted\nvalue ran up to roughly 4.19 million instead of 0..1024 -- a factor of\nabout 4096. Reported in #812, where users worked around it by scaling\noutput_scale down by the same factor.\n\nRead the pin with the Arduino core''s analogReadMilliVolts(), which\napplies the ESP-IDF factory calibration that the removed code used to\nperform, and normalize the result against a reference voltage so that\nread() returns 0..1 again. The reference defaults to 3300 mV and is now\na constructor parameter. Normalizing against a voltage rather than a raw\nbit width keeps the result independent of ADC resolution, which differs\nbetween ESP32 variants -- the portability problem behind #730.\n\nAlso give BaseAnalogReader a virtual destructor. AnalogInput holds the\nreader in a std::unique_ptr<BaseAnalogReader>, so destroying it through\nthe base pointer was undefined behaviour.\n\nRefs: #812, #730","tree":{"sha":"b96c219b500d59f4393ce025baa0c056f9c42c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/b96c219b500d59f4393ce025baa0c056f9c42c38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/375d0db35a02821f5313d251bc23f79bfb6224b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3332251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KEGustafsson","id":3332251,"login":"KEGustafsson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzIyNTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KEGustafsson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/375d0db35a02821f5313d251