iras/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/fb87940226175116834903f299587871233cdc23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T08:34:29Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T09:18:31Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"fix(signalk): make WS buffer size configurable; drop oversize deltas\n\nesp_websocket_client was configured with a hardcoded buffer_size = 1024.\nA delta longer than the buffer is sent as several non-blocking (0-tick)\ntransport writes; when a later write is not instantly accepted,\nesp_websocket_client aborts the connection, freezing every delta during the\nreconnect backoff. Any device whose connect-time sendMeta=all delta or a\nlarge value delta (a GNSS receiver''s full-sky satellitesInView) exceeds 1 KB\ntrips this on nearly every connect.\n\n- Make the buffer size a build-flag-overridable SENSESP_SK_WS_BUFFER_SIZE\n  (default 1024, unchanged). esp_websocket_client allocates it for both tx and\n  rx, so it stays small by default for memory-constrained boards; a device\n  that sends large deltas raises it (-D SENSESP_SK_WS_BUFFER_SIZE=8192).\n\n- Drop a delta longer than the buffer in send_delta() instead of letting the\n  multi-write send abort the connection. The drop does not re-arm metadata: an\n  oversize delta is deterministic, so re-arming would have get_deltas() rebuild\n  the same oversize first delta every cycle, dropped and re-armed forever.\n  Leaving metadata marked sent lets the next, metadata-free first delta fit and\n  flow; metadata waits for a reconnect or a larger buffer. The drop warning is\n  rate-limited so a persistently oversize delta cannot flood the log.\n\nThe drop boundary is a pure predicate (sk_delta_exceeds_ws_buffer) with a host\ntest: a delta of exactly buffer_size sends as a single chunk; only a longer one\nwould split into multiple writes and abort.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdc99f1e776ec7240f34b76433363a2916beaf37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/bdc99f1e776ec7240f34b76433363a2916beaf37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/fb87940226175116834903f299587871233cdc23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url"