eceived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/8c9c7a3f449574b0dc33251bfa989ea3be087f48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T12:22:16Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T12:22:16Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"docs(signalk): drop stale \"SKWSClient task\" section labels\n\nThe dedicated SKWSClient task was removed in the fold; relabel the method\nsections so they don''t reference a task that no longer exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7eeea2f79cce9b50d9304fde950f622e5e4d021d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/7eeea2f79cce9b50d9304fde950f622e5e4d021d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/8c9c7a3f449574b0dc33251bfa989ea3be087f48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/8c9c7a3f449574b0dc33251bfa989ea3be087f48","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDhjOWM3YTNmNDQ5NTc0YjBkYzMzMjUxYmZhOTg5ZWEzYmUwODdmNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b","sha":"dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b"}],"sha":"8c9c7a3f449574b0dc33251bfa989ea3be087f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/8c9c7a3f449574b0dc33251bfa989ea3be087f48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T12:19:57Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T12:19:57Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"refactor(signalk): fold the SK client onto the event loop, delete its task\n\nReplace the dedicated SKWSClient FreeRTOS task (a 100 ms poll loop) with an\nevent_loop()->onRepeat(100) that runs the connect-check + send_delta, and\ndelete ExecuteWebSocketTask. With the prior commits this is safe: connect()\nis a non-blocking dispatcher (blocking auth legs run on a one-shot worker),\nsend_delta() is a 0-timeout send, and teardown is detached -- so nothing on\nthe loop blocks.\n\nThe OOM path of the detached teardown is made non-blocking too: if the\nreaper task can''t be spawned, the handle is stashed (pending_teardown_) and\nthe spawn retried on the next loop tick, instead of a ~1 s synchronous\nstop()+destroy() that would otherwise stall the shared loop under the very\nheap pressure that path exists for.\n\nThis closes the send-vs-teardown lifetime window the B review tracked:\nsend_delta/sendTXT now run on the loop, serialized with detach_teardown\n(same context); transport-task senders (subscribe_listeners,\non_receive_put''s response) are safe because esp_websocket_client_stop()\njoins the transport task before destroy() frees the struct.\n\nReclaims the ~8 KB persistent task stack.\n\nVerified on a HALSER: heartbeat holds dt=1000 ms through connect attempts\nand forced restart() cycles now running on the event loop (the loop-stall\ntest), heap stable and ~8 KB higher with the task gone, no crash. The\nconnected-state soak (deltas flowing while folded + cold-token reacquire)\nis gated on a stable LAN and to be confirmed there.\n\nAdversarial review (loop-stall / lifetime / correctness): GO.\n\nFolds the SK client onto the event loop (SignalK/SensESP#1033).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"52ef8630e632ae1930fb83dca1a5094cfede7f06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/52ef8630e632ae1930fb83dca1a5094cfede7f06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKGRkN2JkZDNiMTU2Mzg1MjNhMjRmN2EzNDk0ZTNjYjQ2OGRhNjk0M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48","sha":"a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48"}],"sha":"dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/dd7bdd3b15638523a24f7a3494e3cb468da6943b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T11:58:54Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T11:58:54Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"fix(signalk): run SK auth/connect on a worker; thread-safe client handle\n\nThe connect()/auth lifecycle made blocking esp_http_client calls\n(access-request, poll, SSL-detect; 10 s timeouts) inline. Split connect()\ninto a non-blocking dispatcher that spawns a one-shot worker task\n(run_connect_attempt) for the blocking legs, guarded by auth_job_running_\nso at most one attempt is in flight. The legs are unchanged; the calling\ncontext (the SK task today, the event loop after the fold) stays responsive.\n\nclient_ is now std::atomic so the worker (which builds it) and the\nSK/event-loop context (which sends on it and reaps it) don''t tear a pointer\nread/write; detach_teardown() reaps via exchange(nullptr), making the\ncheck-and-null a single atomic op (closes the latent double-free the A\nreview flagged). connect_ws builds into a local handle and stores it before\nstart; on start-failure it nulls the shared handle before destroy.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing wedge: poll_access_request could leave the state\nmachine in Authorizing forever on a malformed/unexpected server response (a\ndeserialize error, or a COMPLETED response with an unknown permission) --\nit now falls back to Disconnected to retry. Corrects the restart()/client_\ndoc comments for the atomic handle.\n\nVerified on a HALSER against a real signalk-server: existing-token\nreconnect runs through the worker (connect + forced-restart cycles, flat\nheap, responsive loop); the cold-token attempt runs on the worker with the\nloop responsive through the blocking HTTP and clean recovery. Cold-token\nend-to-end completion (access-request approval -> poll -> connect) is gated\non a stable LAN and will be confirmed in the fold-commit soak.\n\nA residual cross-task send-vs-teardown lifetime window (pre-existing since\nthe teardown was detached) is documented and tracked for the fold commit,\nwhere all sends move onto one context.\n\nPart of running the SK client on the event loop (SignalK/SensESP#1033).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5746b8a03de22ec7d2533864b68a3403ecbd296f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/5746b8a03de22ec7d2533864b68a3403ecbd296f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKGE3ZmY5MmFlMjA5MmY2OWY4NzlmZGViYWVhOTFjODcwMmQ3YTVmNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc","sha":"4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc"}],"sha":"a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/a7ff92ae2092f69f879fdebaea91c8702d7a5f48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T11:28:27Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T11:28:27Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"fix(signalk): make WebSocket teardown non-blocking\n\nrestart() and connect_ws() did a synchronous esp_websocket_client_stop()\n(which waits up to ~1 s for the client task to exit) + destroy(), blocking\nthe caller. Hand the old handle to a detached one-shot task instead, so the\nstop+destroy never runs on the connection context. connect() now reaps a\nstale client at the top and defers bring-up while a reap is in flight, so at\nmost one client exists at a time.\n\nDetaching the teardown lets a dying client (auto_reconnect is left on)\ndispatch a late event into the singleton handler; guard against it with a\ngeneration tag -- the handler is registered with the generation current at\nbuild time and drops any callback whose generation no longer matches.\n\nVerified on a HALSER against a real signalk-server: forcing restart() on a\nhealthy connection every 20 s reconnects cleanly with flat heap across\ncycles (the detached reaper reclaims even a live client) and no loop stall.\n\nrestart() is documented as SK-context-only; swapping client_ atomically (to\nalso make it safe from arbitrary tasks) is deferred to the fold commit,\nwhere the worker-task contexts that touch client_ are introduced.\n\nPart of running the SK client on the event loop (SignalK/SensESP#1033).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85cb98368f91784811c37780ca6db51f2822ed77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/85cb98368f91784811c37780ca6db51f2822ed77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc","node_id":"C_kwDOC0IfMdoAKDRlNzljNWUzMTI0MWEzYjNjOTIwOTM4MmUxNjM2YmI4ZGU4NTg3YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/SensESP/commit/35c3953b16a34492be1e8c95e172fd7c1ce3a6f9","sha":"35c3953b16a34492be1e8c95e172fd7c1ce3a6f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/35c3953b16a34492be1e8c95e172fd7c1ce3a6f9"}],"sha":"4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/4e79c5e31241a3b3c9209382e1636bb8de8587bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mairas","id":407010,"login":"mairas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzAxMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/commits/35c3953b16a34492be1e8c95e172fd7c1ce3a6f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T10:53:38Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T10:53:38Z","email":"matti.airas@hatlabs.fi","name":"Matti Airas"},"message":"fix(signalk): make delta send non-blocking\n\nsend_delta() used a 5 s send timeout and called the blocking restart()\n(esp_websocket_client_stop + destroy) on failure, so it could stall its\ncaller for seconds. Give the periodic delta send its own 0-timeout\nconstant and, on a failed send, drop the rest of the batch instead of\nrestarting: brief ws-client lock contention retries next cycle, and a real\ntransport failure is detected by esp_websocket_client, whose disconnect\nevent already drives reconnect.\n\nFirst step toward running the SK client on the event loop\n(SignalK/SensESP#1033). The control sends (subscribe, PUT, sendTXT) keep\nthe 5 s timeout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d533a938063e895a290d32b39b4b6a030ad41918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/trees/d533a938063e895a290d32b39b4b6a030ad41918"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/SensESP/git/commits/35c3953b16a34492be1e8c95e172fd7c1ce3a6f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/407010?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mairas/events{/privacy}","foll