VhldoAKDM3M2M2NDc1NTQ2NjQ2ZTVlOTk3MzE0ZGJjY2I3MzJlOTQ3MDUzMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commit/90fa3a6ce5fc896be437dedf1567616d28cfe5cf","sha":"90fa3a6ce5fc896be437dedf1567616d28cfe5cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/90fa3a6ce5fc896be437dedf1567616d28cfe5cf"}],"sha":"373c6475546646e5e997314dbccb732e9470532b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/373c6475546646e5e997314dbccb732e9470532b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/90fa3a6ce5fc896be437dedf1567616d28cfe5cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:14:35Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:14:35Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v4.2.0\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) The devices of this adapter are now reachable in the ioBroker Device Manager: each one appears as a card with its name, icon, battery and reachability. Readings are shown on the card itself, and only states that can actually be operated become controls (switch, slider, select), so a read-only device has no control button at all. A control writes to the command state but reads from its feedback partner where the device has one, so a switch shows what the device reports rather than what it was last told. The instance already advertised Device Manager support, but answered none of its requests\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added the \"Clean Light\" theme: white cards on a light grey page with coloured icons, where a tile stays white when its device is on and only the label and the toggle turn blue\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added the \"Tech Blue\" theme: near-black tiles set apart by a lit blue outline, with monochrome blue icons and toggles\n* (@krobipd) Fixed \"Create new folder\" only showing a white screen since 4.0.0 (#679)\n* (@krobipd) Fixed the room column filter emptying the device list: it showed the function filter''s value and wrote the picked room into the function filter (#680)\n* (@krobipd) Fixed an added state being deleted when it was edited without renaming it (#360)\n* (@krobipd) Moving, renaming or copying a device no longer deletes the original when the copy failed halfway through (#151, #513)\n* (@GermanBluefox) A failed copy is only cleaned up when its target path was free beforehand, so renaming a device onto an existing name cannot delete that device''s objects\n* (@krobipd) Manually added states are now deleted together with their device, instead of staying behind as ghost objects after a move, rename or delete (#684)\n* (@krobipd) Cancel in the device editor now really cancels: deleting a state and picking a device icon are applied on Save instead of the moment they are clicked\n* (@krobipd) The read/write function preview shows boolean results and reports an invalid formula, instead of staying empty in both cases (#683)\n* (@krobipd) A string-typed alias no longer inherits `min`/`max`/`step` from its source, which made js-controller warn about an invalid object on every check (#682)\n* (@GermanBluefox) An alias or linked state now takes its type from the source wherever the device type allows more than one, so a thermostat or air conditioner that spells its modes out instead of numbering them is no longer written back as a number (#614). Needs the matching `@iobroker/type-detector` release\n* (@krobipd) A linkeddevices state now inherits the real range of its source instead of a hard 0...100, so a linked thermostat no longer shows 0...100 instead of e.g. 5...35\n* (@krobipd) `TreeView.getDerivedStateFromProps` returns its derived state instead of mutating the state it was handed, which React 19 does not guarantee to keep","tree":{"sha":"47589eb71fa009da996d8688ac2387e2d39a219a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/git/trees/47589eb71fa009da996d8688ac2387e2d39a219a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/git/commits/90fa3a6ce5fc896be437dedf1567616d28cfe5cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred