,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/0dd15051211a2072fec350cca1011ca64548a865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T15:18:13Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T15:18:13Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"message":"fix(widgets): let a climate tile open its dialog at every size\n\n`Thermostat` and `AirCondition` render their dialog inside `renderCompact` and `renderWideTall`. The\n2x0.5 layout comes from the base class, which neither overrides, so at that size the dialog was never\nrendered at all: clicking the tile did nothing, and every control on it — the setpoints, the mode, the\nfan speed, the swing — was unreachable.\n\nBoth now render it beside the tile in a `render()` override, the way `FanBase`, `Pump` and `AirQuality`\nalready do, so it no longer depends on which layouts a widget happens to override.\n\n`Motion` and `Window` each declared a `hideWhenOk` setting that nothing exposed and nothing read — a\ntype promising behaviour the widget does not have. `FireAlarm`, `FloodAlarm` and `Warning` implement it\nproperly and keep theirs. Removing the field left the local `AlarmWidgetSettings` interface with no\nmembers of its own in both, so it goes too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af6cfa53ef01771776d8fcfcf1d00a2b9106d1f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/git/trees/af6cfa53ef01771776d8fcfcf1d00a2b9106d1f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/git/commits/0dd15051211a2072fec350cca1011ca64548a865","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commit/0dd15051211a2072fec350cca1011ca64548a865","node_id":"C_kwDOC7VhldoAKDBkZDE1MDUxMjExYTIwNzJmZWMzNTBjY2ExMDExY2E2NDU0OGE4NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commit/e5e3a3965ade460851061cdee1e7669d40353d20","sha":"e5e3a3965ade460851061cdee1e7669d40353d20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/e5e3a3965ade460851061cdee1e7669d40353d20"}],"sha":"0dd15051211a2072fec350cca1011ca64548a865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/0dd15051211a2072fec350cca1011ca64548a865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/a79d0adc26dce82f1a82c7b4ef5872578c4a21c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T14:41:59Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T14:42:32Z","email":"github@fischer-ka.de","name":"Ingo Fischer"},"message":"feat(widgets): an air-quality tile that ranks what it measures\n\nThe last of the nine device types type-detector 6.0.0 added, and the only one that was ever an\ninformation-design problem rather than plumbing. It has been rendering the generic info tile, which\nshows one value and labels it with whatever the datapoint is named — inadequate for 34 states.\n\nAQI is a band, not a number. The pattern declares it as an enum of seven words, from GOOD to\nEXTREMELY_POOR, so the tile face shows the word and colours it; \"3\" would tell a user nothing. But\nnothing obliges a device to use that enum — adapters report a US-EPA-style 0-500 AQI as a plain number\n— so the label comes from the datapoint''s own `common.states`, then the pattern''s, and a value with\nneither is shown as the number it is. A device reporting 137 reads \"137\", never \"unknown\".\n\nColour is claimed on narrower evidence than the label. A device may use the same 0-6 indices for a\nscale of its own, so a band only tints when the resolved label is one of the seven this scale means.\nThe eleven pollutant levels do trust their 0-4 index, because that domain is the one thing the\ndetector guarantees for them.\n\nThe dialog is what makes eleven concentrations readable: the rows sort by severity, worst first, so\nthe pollutant that matters is at the top instead of wherever the pattern happens to declare it. A row\nwith nothing to rank by — no level state, none reported yet, or one outside the declared enum — sinks\nbelow every readable severity rather than above it. A value nobody can interpret at the top of a list\nthat means \"worst first\" would be worse than no ranking at all.\n\nNothing is presented as better than the evidence supports: a reading that has not arrived is a dash\nand never a zero, UNKNOWN is grey and never green, and a reading from a device that is switched off is\ndimmed on the face as well as in the dialog, because it is the last measurement rather than the air\nnow.\n\nUnits come from the datapoint throughout. Four of the eleven pollutants declare no unit at all, so a\nwidget that assumed one would print something the device never said.\n\nThe ranking and the label-or-number rule are pure logic, extracted so they are tested directly rather\nthan through a rendered tree.\n\nWith this, every one of the nine new types has a purpose-built tile and the info-tile stopgap the bump\nshipped with is retired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46d69db231ae38fc002632beded9f33626d6b550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/git/trees/46d69db231ae38fc002632beded9f33626d6b550"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/git/commits/a79d0adc26dce82f1a82c7b4ef5872578c4a21c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11976694?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Apollon77","id":11976694,"login":"Apollon77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTc2Njk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Apollon77","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commit/a79d0adc26dce82f1a82c7b4ef5872578c4a21c1","node_id":"C_kwDOC7VhldoAKGE3OWQwYWRjMjZkY2U4MmYxYTgyYzdiNGVmNTg3MjU3OGM0YTIxYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commit/e5e3a3965ade460851061cdee1e7669d40353d20","sha":"e5e3a3965ade460851061cdee1e7669d40353d20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/e5e3a3965ade460851061cdee1e7669d40353d20"}],"sha":"a79d0adc26dce82f1a82c7b4ef5872578c4a21c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits/a79d0adc26dce82f1a82c7b4ef5872578c4a21c1"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.devices/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=04625aebba6c8e6a0e66496e75eb11505ba309b1&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A42%3A04.921Z"}');
