Search Graphs\" label on the Graphs overview page and the\n  \"Filter by name\" label in the Import resource tree with `sr-only`.\n- Add a \"Search Graphs\" placeholder to the Graphs overview search field.\n- Update the e2e checks for the two labels.\n\nWhy\nThe visible labels added for accessibility took extra space in the toolbars\nand duplicated the placeholder text. The fields keep their accessible names\nthrough the hidden labels, and the placeholders still tell sighted users\nwhat the fields are for.\n\nTesting\n- graphs.overview.spec.js and import-user-data-file-upload.spec.js pass.","tree":{"sha":"f36c4756a866e9563830e11dab62cfbd2a73fe08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/f36c4756a866e9563830e11dab62cfbd2a73fe08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/ec2e58e332612292adbbbc1b56942c53ca6cee7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/ec2e58e332612292adbbbc1b56942c53ca6cee7b","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKGVjMmU1OGUzMzI2MTIyOTJhZGJiYmMxYjU2OTQyYzUzY2E2Y2VlN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243","sha":"5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243"}],"sha":"ec2e58e332612292adbbbc1b56942c53ca6cee7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/ec2e58e332612292adbbbc1b56942c53ca6cee7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25177016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Brankovanov","id":25177016,"login":"Brankovanov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MTc3MDE2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:19:25Z","email":"georgi.brankovanov@gmail.com","name":"Georgi Brankovanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:19:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"GDB-15293: Secondary cluster index column should not be displayed on multiple line (#3287)\n\nGDB-15293: Secondary cluster index column should not be displayed on\nmultiple line\n\n## What\nThe column displaying the current index of a secondary cluster (in\nmulti-region-table) wraps its content onto multiple lines even when\nthere is enough space to hold it on one line.\n\n## Why\nThe index column header (.tag-index-column) has a fixed width of 16%,\nwhich fixes the width of the whole column. Any longer content wraps even\nwhen the table has free space.\n\n## How\n- Removed the fixed width from the index column header, so the column\ncan grow into any empty space and fit its content. If there is no space\nleft, the content still wraps.\n\n- Added white-space: nowrap; to the column headers in both tables\n(multi-region-table and secondary-tag-table) so they don''t wrap and\nensure consistent behavior on both.\n\n- Set the action column (in multi-region-table) width to 44px when only\nthe delete button is shown, and 85px when the add and cancel buttons are\nshown.\n\n## Testing\n* [x] Workbench build completes without errors.\n* [x] Index column displays long values on a single line when there is\nenough space.\n* [x] Index column wraps content when there is no space left.\n* [x] Column headers do not wrap.\n* [x] Action column is 44px wide with only the delete button, and 85px\nwith add and cancel buttons.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"748\" height=\"943\" alt=\"GDB-15293-index-column-width\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89980b4f-e090-4e72-96d5-132afd7140ef\"\n/>\n\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Branch name\n- [x] Target branch\n- [x] Commit messages\n- [x] Squash commits\n- [x] MR name\n- [x] MR Description\n- [ ] Tests\n- [ ] Browser support verified\n\nCo-authored-by: Georgi Brankovanov <georgi.brankovanov@graphwise.ai>","tree":{"sha":"4ca3e57278c369ba06550469a64b30d6cfc54a25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/4ca3e57278c369ba06550469a64b30d6cfc54a25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ca3e57278c369ba06550469a64b30d6cfc54a25\nparent 49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28\nauthor Georgi Brankovanov <georgi.brankovanov@gmail.com> 1791361165 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361165 +0000\n\nGDB-15293: Secondary cluster index column should not be displayed on multiple line (#3287)\n\nGDB-15293: Secondary cluster index column should not be displayed on\nmultiple line\n\n## What\nThe column displaying the current index of a secondary cluster (in\nmulti-region-table) wraps its content onto multiple lines even when\nthere is enough space to hold it on one line.\n\n## Why\nThe index column header (.tag-index-column) has a fixed width of 16%,\nwhich fixes the width of the whole column. Any longer content wraps even\nwhen the table has free space.\n\n## How\n- Removed the fixed width from the index column header, so the column\ncan grow into any empty space and fit its content. If there is no space\nleft, the content still wraps.\n\n- Added white-space: nowrap; to the column headers in both tables\n(multi-region-table and secondary-tag-table) so they don''t wrap and\nensure consistent behavior on both.\n\n- Set the action column (in multi-region-table) width to 44px when only\nthe delete button is shown, and 85px when the add and cancel buttons are\nshown.\n\n## Testing\n* [x] Workbench build completes without errors.\n* [x] Index column displays long values on a single line when there is\nenough space.\n* [x] Index column wraps content when there is no space left.\n* [x] Column headers do not wrap.\n* [x] Action column is 44px wide with only the delete button, and 85px\nwith add and cancel buttons.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"748\" height=\"943\" alt=\"GDB-15293-index-column-width\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89980b4f-e090-4e72-96d5-132afd7140ef\"\n/>\n\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Branch name\n- [x] Target branch\n- [x] Commit messages\n- [x] Squash commits\n- [x] MR name\n- [x] MR Description\n- [ ] Tests\n- [ ] Browser support verified\n\nCo-authored-by: Georgi Brankovanov <georgi.brankovanov@graphwise.ai>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgCNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwzUQAJ3eaC/dsb06hR+2W6boXMiM\nn4AAQl31kf/PskjPcQ99TydudopdHuYoSgkNym6C22tgbfSi//368RK3f2g9PLEw\nJVsCip+bGkfczRl8qDTaa363RTAZ2Q8lfPpRshy8pTv2oTTqxwwQW4PDQkOypOBQ\nJruWAWnFT5eXUjdK2nu814aQMNkkUGjH8RvE92QZtowIh71yY5USwj0FVcuj93EU\nlS680jCYyiYtIHjZumMKd3cC6NfVHrwbx/8zcLmCiPgVbl1hWAVzmrMMzMpF2r3E\nXLPFmeJHAtWOafZw8LfhAcaOMmSbjLGEyHHSlXNMCXXcbQBl+FqTtFaz/aqUkHii\nXAg9O9OtObMlZB/vs/RfmTeIrQ1npLWi6FmydSF4jk90QFLVmAhEj93l+MelLQ97\nrAChJCmYkkQY3FG7hMdRamYegfgcvdQiyXda8/OFAiUxJJbQD/BSYlOYDSnhZxwk\npZoirBL2ZxKhXMlApFMah/xb8kS6nyO91kNVm/ulreIrRKzyvikKiPrJf+SteLpR\n+/IZ8dCXwjSFYOkNV4t8ZiOgqDP3doILzxAS3rU/jjCQbEwgJGoOMKF9/6/Rzpc6\newXeyfxT7TzHb7l0CTjMO33a2LHzzjekbcw9Es+l+l8MeZo2Zi3yRtb5dGO3gh5U\nklx3EuTlRqnOqtTcKllY\n=qG14\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:19:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDVjZGJmODU2ZjliNTlmMTljNjY0NjhjNDI3ZWFiZDI4ODFmODgyNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28","sha":"49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28"}],"sha":"5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/5cdbf856f9b59f19c66468c427eabd2881f88243"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:12:33Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@graphwise.ai","name":"Plamen Yordanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:16:25Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@ontotext.com","name":"plamen-yordanov"},"message":"GDB-15332 make reactodia use whole screen height\n\n## What\nMake Reactodia use the whole screen height.\n\n## Why\nThe `graphwise-reactodia` host had a fixed `height: 75vh`, so the diagram never filled the space the host page gives it.\n\n## How\nAdded `flex: 1` to the wrapper div, so it grows\n\n## Testing\nn/a","tree":{"sha":"eea2dc7f7898fb8922ae890eec6d4888b228f989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/eea2dc7f7898fb8922ae890eec6d4888b228f989"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190497925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/plamen-yordanov","id":190497925,"login":"plamen-yordanov","node_id":"U_kgDOC1rEhQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDQ5OTM1ZmQ2OGFlOGQ3Yjc2MDkxOWMxMmEwYzRkNjkxYTU4ZTljMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5","sha":"f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5"}],"sha":"49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/49935fd68ae8d7b760919c12a0c4d691a58e9c28"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:18:27Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@graphwise.ai","name":"Plamen Yordanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:58:43Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@ontotext.com","name":"plamen-yordanov"},"message":"GDB-15335 rename reactodia to graph navigator\n\n## What\nRename Reactodia to Graph Navigator.\n\n## Why\nThe workbench showed \"Reactodia\", the name of the underlying library, as the name of the view. It appeared in the menu, the view title, the help text, the resource view and SPARQL editor buttons and radio options, and the `/reactodia` URL. Users should see the product name \"Graph Navigator\" instead.\n\n## How\n- Changed the user-facing translations in `shared-components`, `workbench` and `legacy-workbench` (en and fr) to \"Graph Navigator\" and \"Visualize Graph Navigator\".\n- Renamed the route from `reactodia` to `graph-navigator` in `app.routes.ts`, `workbench-routes-provider.ts`, the menu `plugin.js`, `UriUtil.REACTODIA_URL` and every navigation call that opens the view.\n- Added \"Graph Navigator\" to the identical translations in both `validate-translations.js` scripts, replacing the trailing-space workaround in the fr bundles.\n- Renamed the view-related helpers (`goToGraphNavigator`, `navigateToGraphNavigator`, `exploreGraphNavigator*`) in the files touched above.\n- Updated the test wording, `VIEW_URL` and the sample paths in `routing-utils.spec.ts`.\n\n## Testing\njest, cypress","tree":{"sha":"b06c32dbc0c33aa04a8d69a7c4315f5d47178536","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/b06c32dbc0c33aa04a8d69a7c4315f5d47178536"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190497925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/plamen-yordanov","id":190497925,"login":"plamen-yordanov","node_id":"U_kgDOC1rEhQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKGYzMzQzMjAyMTYwMzFiZDRkZDc5N2Y4MjRhNjQxM2ZmYWM0YzBlYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/1efb56507cb238b0af10f078dc8639c362b29363","sha":"1efb56507cb238b0af10f078dc8639c362b29363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/1efb56507cb238b0af10f078dc8639c362b29363"}],"sha":"f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/f334320216031bd4dd797f824a6413ffac4c0eb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25177016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Brankovanov","id":25177016,"login":"Brankovanov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MTc3MDE2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brankovanov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/1efb56507cb238b0af10f078dc8639c362b29363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:34:38Z","email":"georgi.brankovanov@gmail.com","name":"Georgi Brankovanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:34:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"GDB-14670: Stop repositories from starting on hover (#3255)\n\nDB-14670: Stop repositories from starting on hover\n\n## What\n\nHovering over a repository for a second or two on the repositories page\nor in the repository picker opens the repository popover, which calls\nthe /size endpoint. The popover needs this data to show the number of\nstatements. As a side effect, the call activates the repository if it is\nin the INACTIVE state.\n\n## Why\n\nThe /size endpoint requires the repository to be running to return\nstatement statistics. As a result, INACTIVE repositories are started\nwhen users only hover over them.\n\n## How\n\nUpdate the templates and logic of the repository visualizations\n(repositories page and repository picker) so that the /size endpoint is\nnot called for repositories that are not in the RUNNING state when the\npopover is displayed.\n\nUpdate the repository popover template and logic so that the repository\nstate is shown, with two different templates: one for repositories in\nthe RUNNING state and one for repositories in any other state.\n\nUpdate the repository popover logic so that it refreshes when the state\nof the targeted repository changes (repositories page only).\n\n##Testing\n\n* [x] Workbench build completes without errors.\n* [x] Popover styles and templates match the provided designs.\n* [x] The /size endpoint is not called for repositories that are not in\nthe RUNNING state.\n* [x] The correct popover template is displayed for repositories in the\nRUNNING state and for those in other states.\n* [x] The popover updates when the repository state changes on the\nrepositories page.\n\n## Screenshots\n \n<img width=\"1179\" height=\"518\" alt=\"GDB-14670-repository-page-popover\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcab9a25-90c5-4d6f-bf0e-76e37149e4f9\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1174\" height=\"512\" alt=\"GDB-14670-repository-picker-popover\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6165751-8cad-494b-ba04-e5524f3491de\"\n/>\n\n## Checklist\n\n* [x] Branch name\n* [x] Target branch\n* [x] Commit messages\n* [x] Squash commits\n* [x] MR name\n* [x] MR description\n* [ ] Tests\n* [ ] Browser support verified\n\nCo-authored-by: Georgi Brankovanov <georgi.brankovanov@graphwise.ai>","tree":{"sha":"95f07f794377e6140ba59d127ae85d9d7a9f02cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/95f07f794377e6140ba59d127ae85d9d7a9f02cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/1efb56507cb238b0af10f078dc8639c362b29363","verification":{"payload":"tree 95f07f794377e6140ba59d127ae85d9d7a9f02cc\nparent 8ce0826b0c3395bf5d9708fd673b728b94073c10\nauthor Georgi Brankovanov <georgi.brankovanov@gmail.com> 1791286478 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791286478 +0000\n\nGDB-14670: Stop repositories from starting on hover (#3255)\n\nDB-14670: Stop repositories from starting on hover\n\n## What\n\nHovering over a repository for a second or two on the repositories page\nor in the repository picker opens the repository popover, which calls\nthe /size endpoint. The popover needs this data to show the number of\nstatements. As a side effect, the call activates the repository if it is\nin the INACTIVE state.\n\n## Why\n\nThe /size endpoint requires the repository to be running to return\nstatement statistics. As a result, INACTIVE repositories are started\nwhen users only hover over them.\n\n## How\n\nUpdate the templates and logic of the repository visualizations\n(repositories page and repository picker) so that the /size endpoint is\nnot called for repositories that are not in the RUNNING state when the\npopover is displayed.\n\nUpdate the repository popover template and logic so that the repository\nstate is shown, with two different templates: one for repositories in\nthe RUNNING state and one for repositories in any other state.\n\nUpdate the repository popover logic so that it refreshes when the state\nof the targeted repository changes (repositories page only).\n\n##Testing\n\n* [x] Workbench build completes without errors.\n* [x] Popover styles and templates match the provided designs.\n* [x] The /size endpoint is not called for repositories that are not in\nthe RUNNING state.\n* [x] The correct popover template is displayed for repositories in the\nRUNNING state and for those in other states.\n* [x] The popover updates when the repository state changes on the\nrepositories page.\n\n## Screenshots\n \n<img width=\"1179\" height=\"518\" alt=\"GDB-14670-repository-page-popover\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcab9a25-90c5-4d6f-bf0e-76e37149e4f9\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1174\" height=\"512\" alt=\"GDB-14670-repository-picker-popover\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6165751-8cad-494b-ba04-e5524f3491de\"\n/>\n\n## Checklist\n\n* [x] Branch name\n* [x] Target branch\n* [x] Commit messages\n* [x] Squash commits\n* [x] MR name\n* [x] MR description\n* [ ] Tests\n* [ ] Browser support verified\n\nCo-authored-by: Georgi Brankovanov <georgi.brankovanov@graphwise.ai>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNzOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWXQQADSks5aQ5RqVZsnG5g0hLMAZ\neXo1yJ20zMdp5LqZRsjPZanKwptUBozEhuFaptS882G5gVZ/75/F6yTQ2tfOnEIx\nY2nLSQtoZrJpZoG00/N/ZtPYoIcJJg/V3MTBv6oG79yP8Cux5M/0GfnQ/Cy7Q