"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/99201ce3813851451cc25925d8224d5b83643e15","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDk5MjAxY2UzODEzODUxNDUxY2MyNTkyNWQ4MjI0ZDViODM2NDNlMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e","sha":"fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e"}],"sha":"99201ce3813851451cc25925d8224d5b83643e15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/99201ce3813851451cc25925d8224d5b83643e15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108174872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boyan-tonchev","id":108174872,"login":"boyan-tonchev","node_id":"U_kgDOBnKeGA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:23:53Z","email":"boyan.tonchev@graphwise.ai","name":"boyan.tonchev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:36:13Z","email":"108174872+boyan-tonchev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Boyan Tonchev"},"message":"GDB-15284: Add component level tests for page restrictions and repository picker list\n\n## What\nAdded component level tests for the page restrictions and the repository picker list.\n\n## Why\nThe page restriction behaviour was only partly covered, by tests spread across separate component specs.\n\n## How\nTesting it through the page layout covers the real flow (license, security, repositories, selected\nrepository and declared restrictions together) as the manual test scenarios describe it, so regressions\nin the restrictions and the repository picker list are caught automatically.\n\nThe tests are driven by scenarios: each one describes the input (license, user, repositories, selected\nrepository and declared restrictions) and the expected result (shown content, restriction messages,\npicker and create button). The scenarios are created with a dedicated builder, which keeps them short\nand readable and generates each scenario''s description from its input.","tree":{"sha":"5ef1825814e0d8b193e5e5d5065c4f72c8c67255","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/5ef1825814e0d8b193e5e5d5065c4f72c8c67255"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108174872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boyan-tonchev","id":108174872,"login":"boyan-tonchev","node_id":"U_kgDOBnKeGA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKGZiZjMwMjUwNjQ4YmFmMTcwOGEzNmEyYWM5ZGRkY2Y0YTUyOWQ2MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85","sha":"1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85"}],"sha":"fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/fbf30250648baf1708a36a2ac9dddcf4a529d61e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:40:10Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:16:03Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15266: Extract import page getters into steps\n\nMove the selectors used by the accessible names test into getters in\nImportSteps and reuse them in the existing row actions.","tree":{"sha":"e6cf291efa14e9d52164a973c8827c6845e74bdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/e6cf291efa14e9d52164a973c8827c6845e74bdf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDFlZDI3MTYyNjFjYjAzOTM4OWFlYzBmMWYyOTJiNGU2MWQwZDRlODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db","sha":"2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db"}],"sha":"1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/1ed2716261cb039389aec0f1f292b4e61d0d4e85"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:15:28Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:16:03Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15266: Add accessible names and labels on the Import page\n\nWhat\n- Give the icon-only buttons on the Import page an `aria-label`: the help\n  toggle, and the reset status, remove and import actions in each resource\n  row. Their icons are marked `aria-hidden`.\n- Give the row selection checkbox an `aria-label` with the resource path.\n- Name the status dropdown after its purpose, and include the selected\n  status when there is one.\n- Add a visible \"Filter by name\" label to the resource filter field.\n- Render the context link only when the resource has a context.\n- Replace the upload label that pointed to the file input generated by\n  ng-file-upload with a plain element.\n\nWhy\nThe IBM Equal Access Checker reported `input_label_exists` for the icon-only\nbuttons and the row checkbox, `input_label_visible` for the status dropdown\nand for the filter field, which had only a placeholder, `a_text_purpose` for\nempty context links, and `label_ref_valid` for the upload label.\n\nThe context link used `if` instead of `ng-if`, so an empty link was rendered\nfor every resource without a context.\n\nThe upload label pointed to the hidden input that ng-file-upload appends to\nthe body, which the checker does not accept as a valid target.\n\nHow\n- The row labels contain the resource path, so the actions are\n  distinguishable per row, also in the tree view.\n- The help button reuses its tooltip translation key. The row actions and the\n  status dropdown use new parameterised keys in English and French.\n- The e2e upload step selects the generated input by its ID instead of\n  through the removed label.\n\nTesting\n- `npm run lint` and `npm run validate` pass.\n- The IBM Equal Access engine (`IBM_Accessibility` policy) reports no\n  failures for the phase 1 rules on Import (User data tab) with files that are\n  not imported, imported with a named graph and imported into the default\n  graph. The help button is still reported as \"needs review\" for\n  `input_label_visible`, because its name comes from `aria-label`.\n- `import-user-data-file-upload.spec.js` (with a new test for the accessible\n  names), `import-view.spec.js` and\n  `import-server-files-batch-operations.spec.js` pass.","tree":{"sha":"c7d807a768824ae0384e30628d9bea9ac992c3a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/c7d807a768824ae0384e30628d9bea9ac992c3a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDJlMWUxNzEzMThiZjZmZGM5Njk3NDEzNmMwNjNhOGNhMjcwYzE3ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe","sha":"0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe"}],"sha":"2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/2e1e171318bf6fdc96974136c063a8ca270c17db"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:53:27Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:59:12Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15202: Fix vulnerable dependencies\n\nWhat\n- Bump puppeteer to ^25.12.0 in shared-components and accessibilty-audit,\n  and lighthouse to ^13.5.0 in accessibilty-audit.\n- Remove unused puppeteer and babel-preset-es2015 from legacy-workbench.\n- Bump @angular/* runtime packages to ^21.2.25 in workbench.\n- Add npm overrides for vulnerable transitive dependencies:\n  - workbench: piscina ^5.3.2, uuid ^11.1.1 (under sockjs)\n  - e2e-tests: js-yaml@^3 -> ^3.15.2, uuid ^11.1.1 (under\n    istanbul-lib-processinfo), undici ^6.29.0 (under @actions/http-client)\n- Refresh lock files.\n\nWhy\nnpm audit reported critical and high severity vulnerabilities (piscina RCE,\nbabel-traverse code execution, extract-zip path traversal, @angular/router\nDoS, etc.).\n\nHow\nUpgraded direct dependencies where a patched version exists, removed unused\nones, and used scoped overrides where the parent package pins a vulnerable\nversion that has a compatible patched release. Remaining findings (braces,\nnode-forge, AngularJS, echarts 6, elliptic) have no compatible fix.\n\nTesting\n- npm run build passes.\n- npm run test passes for all packages.","tree":{"sha":"61a28595ec05f56fed75020d86fdd58230c38de6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/61a28595ec05f56fed75020d86fdd58230c38de6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDA2MzlhMDY1YTEwZTQ2M2YxOGU4ZmQwZjU0YTk1MTA2YmU4ZTE4ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a","sha":"8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a"}],"sha":"0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/0639a065a10e463f18e8fd0f54a95106be8e18fe"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:15:08Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:49:30Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15269: Add accessible names on the Repositories page\n\nWhat\n- Give every icon-only button and link on the Repositories page an\n  `aria-label`: common settings, license, edit and detach location, copy URL,\n  edit, download config, restart, delete and set as default repository.\n- Row actions and location actions include the repository id or location in\n  their name, so they can be told apart.\n- Give the connect `span role=\"button\"` the name \"Connect repository {{id}}\"\n  and expose its state with `aria-pressed`. The \"Set as default repository\"\n  toggle also exposes its state with `aria-pressed`.\n- FedX members list: label the edit, remove and set as writable buttons with\n  the member name, and expose the writable state with `aria-pressed`.\n- Mark the icons inside these controls `aria-hidden`.\n\nWhy\nThe IBM Equal Access Checker reported `input_label_exists` and\n`a_text_purpose` for the icon-only buttons and links, and Lighthouse reported\n`aria-command-name` for the connect buttons.\n\nHow\n- Controls without a per-row target reuse their tooltip translation keys.\n  Per-row labels use new parameterised keys in English and French, so the\n  word order is correct in both languages.\n- In the FedX members list, `ng-click`, `ng-if` and the tooltip move from the\n  inner icon to the button, so the buttons work from the keyboard. The\n  writable button gets `type=\"button\"`, so it no longer submits the form.\n\nTesting\n- `npm run lint` and `npm run validate` pass.\n- The IBM Equal Access engine (`IBM_Accessibility` policy) reports no\n  `input_label_exists` or `a_text_purpose` failures on Repositories with six\n  repositories. The remaining findings are `table_headers_exists` and\n  `target_spacing_sufficient`.\n- Checked in the browser that the labels render in English and French and\n  that `aria-pressed` follows the connect, default and writable toggles.","tree":{"sha":"7195f25e5c6597aa78da5b2b7c0dd846f08d22da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/7195f25e5c6597aa78da5b2b7c0dd846f08d22da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDhhYWMzNThkZTc2ZjIzNWI0Yjk3YTdmMTdhZDY3N2JhODMzZTZjNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9","sha":"7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9"}],"sha":"8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/8aac358de76f235b4b97a7f17ad677ba833e6c4a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:05:47Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@graphwise.ai","name":"Plamen Yordanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:10:16Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@ontotext.com","name":"plamen-yordanov"},"message":"GDB-15344 expose overridable theming variables\n\n## What\nExpose overridable theming variables.\n\n## Why\nSo the wrapper is not coupled to any client\n\n## How\n- Added `style-partials/_reactodia-theme.scss` to the `reactodia-component-facade`, mapping each `--graphwise-reactodia-type-color-*` property to its `--gw-foreground-visual-diagram-categorical-*` token at `:root`. That way the node colours stay the same as before.\n- Changed `reactodia-component-facade.component.scss` to `@use` the partial. That way the mapping is applied while the facade is rendered.\n\n## Testing\nn/a","tree":{"sha":"2f456b8c0056d477c8ac1151ff104784a8dabce9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/2f456b8c0056d477c8ac1151ff104784a8dabce9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190497925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/plamen-yordanov","id":190497925,"login":"plamen-yordanov","node_id":"U_kgDOC1rEhQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDdkOTFmMjQ0MmYwN2ZiODgwOGFmOWNiNmY3ODk5Mzk3NjlhMzY4Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2","sha":"a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2"}],"sha":"7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/7d91f2442f07fb8808af9cb6f789939769a368f9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:55:57Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@graphwise.ai","name":"Plamen Yordanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T05:54:08Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@ontotext.com","name":"plamen-yordanov"},"message":"fix comments","tree":{"sha":"b177c46b020065d6013c6f250a4fd6190501808d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/b177c46b020065d6013c6f250a4fd6190501808d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190497925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/plamen-yordanov","id":190497925,"login":"plamen-yordanov","node_id":"U_kgDOC1rEhQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKGE2MjI0N2M2MzRmZDdkYzBiYjljODJmMjMyYWU0NDZlMDJmMmNiZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96","sha":"552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96"}],"sha":"a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/a62247c634fd7dc0bb9c82f232ae446e02f2cbd2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:13:51Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@graphwise.ai","name":"Plamen Yordanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T05:54:08Z","email":"plamen.yordanov@ontotext.com","name":"plamen-yordanov"},"message":"GDB-15257 implement upload and export settings functionality\n\n## What\nImplement upload and export settings functionality for the Reactodia graph navigator.\n\n## Why\nTo give the user the ability to define repository specific settings, which are better suited than the default ones\n\n## How\n- Add the `graph-navigator` API domain: `GraphNavigatorSettings` and `SparqlDataProviderSettings` models, `GraphNavigatorService` with `getSettings`, `uploadSettings`, `deleteSettings` and\n `exportSettings`, a `GraphNavigatorRestService` stubbed until `GDB-15242`, the response type and its mapper, exported from `ontotext-workbench-api.ts`.\n- Add `ReactodiaSettingsComponent`: a Settings button and popover with upload, export and reset, confirming the destructive actions and emitting them to the page.\n- Make `ReactodiaPageComponent` own the settings — load them on repository change, discard late responses, run the upload/reset/export requests, report success and backend errors via toastr, save the export with `file-saver`, and render the facade only once the settings are loaded.\n- Pass the settings to `graphwise-reactodia` through the new `providerSettings` input of\n    `ReactodiaComponentFacadeComponent`.\n- Add the `canMaintainActiveRepo` permission to `RestrictAccessDirective` and gate the settings controls with it.\n\n  ## Testing\n  `jest`, `cypress`","tree":{"sha":"38e2237ac742f6a13787aca76060600f572e7545","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/38e2237ac742f6a13787aca76060600f572e7545"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190497925?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/plamen-yordanov","id":190497925,"login":"plamen-yordanov","node_id":"U_kgDOC1rEhQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plamen-yordanov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDU1MmY2NjFlNTVlODU1MDYwNDEwMTdkNDE3M2UyZjYxYjJiZjBmOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e","sha":"c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e"}],"sha":"552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/552f661e55e85506041017d4173e2f61b2bf0f96"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:27:53Z","email":"ubuntu@ip-10-0-128-211.eu-west-1.compute.internal","name":"Ubuntu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:27:53Z","email":"ubuntu@ip-10-0-128-211.eu-west-1.compute.internal","name":"Ubuntu"},"message":"Release 4.0.0-TR8","tree":{"sha":"3516d788f9ae0c5c4cac54604ce2175d506f9efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/3516d788f9ae0c5c4cac54604ce2175d506f9efe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKGM2OWE4NTc5NDYxMjQzMGY4YjFmM2RiYmZhNmZiYzVmMzRhN2Y0MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149","sha":"3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149"}],"sha":"c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/c69a85794612430f8b1f3dbbfa6fbc5f34a7f41e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:58:52Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:37:33Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15265: Add accessible names and labels on the Home page\n\nWhat\n- Give the copy URL, edit and refresh buttons on the active repository\n  card an `aria-label`. Each one reuses its `gdb-tooltip` translation key.\n  Their icons are marked `aria-hidden`.\n- Give the clear button of the `search-resource-input` directive an\n  `aria-label`, reusing its tooltip key. Make it work from the keyboard.\n- Add an optional `labelled-by` attribute to the `search-resource-input`\n  directive. It sets `aria-labelledby` on the search input.\n- On Home, point the RDF resource search input to the visible\n  \"View resource\" heading.\n\nWhy\nThe IBM Equal Access Checker reported `input_label_exists` for the icon-only\nbuttons. The clear button is included because it appears once the search\ninput has text. The checker reported `input_label_visible` for the search\ninput, which was labelled only by its placeholder, and the placeholder\ndisappears once the user types.\n\nThe clear handler was bound to the icon inside the button, so pressing\nEnter or Space on the focused button did nothing.\n\nHow\n- The search input takes its name from the heading already shown above it,\n  so the layout does not change.\n- `aria-labelledby` is rendered only when `labelled-by` is set. The other\n  pages that use the directive are unchanged.\n- The clear handler is now on the button, which also gets\n  `type=\"button\"`. The button is removed once the input is empty, so\n  clicking it moves the focus back to the input.\n\nTesting\n- `npm run lint` and `npm run validate` pass.\n- The IBM Equal Access engine (`accessibility-checker-engine`,\n  `IBM_Accessibility` policy) reports 0 violations on Home with an active\n  repository, both with an empty search input and with text entered.\n- Enter, Space and a mouse click on the clear button empty the input and\n  leave the focus on it.\n- `e2e-legacy/home/rdf-resource-search.spec.js` passes.\n- On Graphs visualizations, no `aria-labelledby` is rendered.","tree":{"sha":"58ef4a789e253e1b7a01a12dd067d840994e3775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/58ef4a789e253e1b7a01a12dd067d840994e3775"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDM3NjBkMmFkMzQ4Zjc3MDRmN2E1MWNmYmQyOTVkYTY5NjQzOWExNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647","sha":"e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647"}],"sha":"3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/3760d2ad348f7704f7a51cfbd295da696439a149"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108174872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boyan-tonchev","id":108174872,"login":"boyan-tonchev","node_id":"U_kgDOBnKeGA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:30:56Z","email":"boyan.tonchev@graphwise.ai","name":"boyan.tonchev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:07:01Z","email":"108174872+boyan-tonchev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Boyan Tonchev"},"message":"# GDB-15286: Fix writable repository checks for Ontop repositories\n\n## What\nThe fetched writable repositories included repositories that are not actually writable.\n\n## Why\nThe legacy functionality filters out Ontop repositories because they are read-only. This logic was not implemented in the new Workbench because we wanted to investigate the reason behind it and decide whether it was still needed.\n\nThe misleading part is that users can be created or updated with write permissions for Ontop repositories, even though these repositories are read-only.\n\n## How\n- Moved all repository-related methods from `authorization.service.ts` to `repository.service.ts` because they filter repositories based on repository-specific data. `authorization.service.ts` should only handle user permissions for repositories.\n- Added filtering to the methods that fetch repositories with write permissions, excluding Ontop repositories.","tree":{"sha":"cd0c8b497b87f5bac8ab05a09e36f0f11e3deb21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/cd0c8b497b87f5bac8ab05a09e36f0f11e3deb21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108174872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boyan-tonchev","id":108174872,"login":"boyan-tonchev","node_id":"U_kgDOBnKeGA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKGU1NGQ5NDgwYzQ2NDYzMzVjYzViOTM1MjhmZTEyN2ZmZmY1NmM2NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45","sha":"45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45"}],"sha":"e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/e54d9480c4646335cc5b93528fe127ffff56c647"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:26:54Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T07:08:55Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15264: Fix invalid ARIA ID references\n\nWhat\n- Replace all 32 free-text `aria-describedby` values in legacy-workbench\n  templates with valid accessible names.\n- Tables with a visible heading now use `aria-labelledby`, pointing to an\n  `id` added to that heading.\n- All other tables use `aria-label` with a translated key. The new keys are\n  in `en` and `fr`, under each feature''s existing namespace.\n\nWhy\n`aria-describedby` must reference existing, unique element IDs. The IBM\nEqual Access Checker reported `aria_id_unique` violations (WCAG 4.1.2) on\nRepositories, Graphs Overview and Settings, and the same pattern existed\nacross the rest of the legacy UI.\n\nHow\n- Tables rendered inside `ng-repeat` use `aria-label` to avoid duplicate IDs.\n- The local location table reuses the existing\n  `repositories.location.local.graph_db.instance` key.\n\nTesting\n- `grep -rn ''aria-describedby'' packages/legacy-workbench/src` returns nothing.\n- `npm run validate` and `npm run lint` pass.","tree":{"sha":"7b8442b9fdacb3880524b1bbb4f9c9ee53153d6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/7b8442b9fdacb3880524b1bbb4f9c9ee53153d6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDQ1NTczYzcyZDNkM2YxZDZhNjU5MTMyYThiY2RjNThiY2M1NjFmNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4","sha":"995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4"}],"sha":"45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/45573c72d3d3f1d6a659132a8bcdc58bcc561f45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108174872?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boyan-tonchev","id":108174872,"login":"boyan-tonchev","node_id":"U_kgDOBnKeGA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boyan-tonchev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:43:56Z","email":"108174872+boyan-tonchev@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Boyan Tonchev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:43:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"GDB-14749: Expose isRestricted check in the new workbench. (#3241)\n\n## What\nIntroduces a shared view-restriction mechanism for the new workbench.\nRoutes declare the restriction conditions and repository requirements\nthat apply to them, and the workbench uses this information to determine\nwhether the view content can be shown or whether the restriction block\nshould be displayed.\n\nThe mechanism also ensures that the repository picker only offers\nrepositories compatible with the current view.\n\n## Why\n`PageRestrictionsComponent` already had the UI and the logic to turn a\nrestricted state into user-facing messages, but nothing drove it: its\n`isRestricted` signal was never updated, so the restriction state could\nnot reflect the actual application state.\n\nThis implements the missing restriction mechanism while keeping the UI\ncomponents responsible only for displaying the resulting state.\n\n## How\n- A route declares the restriction conditions and repository\nrequirements in its `WorkbenchRouteData`. `AppComponent` reads this\ninformation on navigation and stores it in a shared\n`RestrictionContextService`.\n- A new `ViewRestrictionService` determines whether the current view is\nrestricted based on the declared conditions and whether the selected\nrepository meets the view''s requirements.\n- The restriction state is recalculated whenever relevant application\nstate changes, including navigation, repository, license, security, and\nauthenticated-user changes.\n- `PageRestrictionsComponent` and `PageLayoutComponent` consume the\nshared restriction state and display the restriction messages and\nrepository picker instead of the page content when necessary.\n- The repository picker is also filtered according to the repository\nrequirements declared by the current view, ensuring that repositories\nincompatible with the view are not offered.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Branch name\n- [x] Target branch\n- [x] Commit messages\n- [x] Squash commits\n- [x] MR name\n- [x] MR Description\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Browser support verified","tree":{"sha":"da32bfab82c8db46a7449bf7cbab81e9533aa206","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/da32bfab82c8db46a7449bf7cbab81e9533aa206"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4","verification":{"payload":"tree da32bfab82c8db46a7449bf7cbab81e9533aa206\nparent 06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103\nauthor Boyan Tonchev <108174872+boyan-tonchev@users.noreply.github.com> 1790761436 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790761436 +0300\n\nGDB-14749: Expose isRestricted check in the new workbench. (#3241)\n\n## What\nIntroduces a shared view-restriction mechanism for the new workbench.\nRoutes declare the restriction conditions and repository requirements\nthat apply to them, and the workbench uses this information to determine\nwhether the view content can be shown or whether the restriction block\nshould be displayed.\n\nThe mechanism also ensures that the repository picker only offers\nrepositories compatible with the current view.\n\n## Why\n`PageRestrictionsComponent` already had the UI and the logic to turn a\nrestricted state into user-facing messages, but nothing drove it: its\n`isRestricted` signal was never updated, so the restriction state could\nnot reflect the actual application state.\n\nThis implements the missing restriction mechanism while keeping the UI\ncomponents responsible only for displaying the resulting state.\n\n## How\n- A route declares the restriction conditions and repository\nrequirements in its `WorkbenchRouteData`. `AppComponent` reads this\ninformation on navigation and stores it in a shared\n`RestrictionContextService`.\n- A new `ViewRestrictionService` determines whether the current view is\nrestricted based on the declared conditions and whether the selected\nrepository meets the view''s requirements.\n- The restriction state is recalculated whenever relevant application\nstate changes, including navigation, repository, license, security, and\nauthenticated-user changes.\n- `PageRestrictionsComponent` and `PageLayoutComponent` consume the\nshared restriction state and display the restriction messages and\nrepository picker instead of the page content when necessary.\n- The repository picker is also filtered according to the repository\nrequirements declared by the current view, ensuring that repositories\nincompatible with the view are not offered.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Branch name\n- [x] Target branch\n- [x] Commit messages\n- [x] Squash commits\n- [x] MR name\n- [x] MR Description\n- [x] Tests\n- [ ] Browser support verified","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvNncCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGv8QAEWm8K8pt2efSfwpV0OCD5vq\ny/k2DLWcYbiNiAqcinzAqWs8y9gOAkrch5QzbamnxylXprMXyTBUxH6FC8U0zyJY\ngQrNck6RDq2k7UIERSqT8xp24gRlfviF50c7yVS8mRxZMIXt++lGDEGA/3Xnuwdt\nSuq2tToaTVB67Kx4htuc33gzDfZOFpa5g+xmcuyy6fpWOUgaUN9z99WIN/WAVyX1\nCPtttClSGUxtwX2KyuU6qpZPWwK/cQAZqeTCqaQvPB+Ue2it9kYF7qkpq7A3M1p9\nho+sGpqHz3v3ukZ0p/8rVh8MFRRAHbqywd3LHAyC4Lp1SUep/7ZAZy7PDdF9qWDx\na92AP8d9c6yP5XSppZLfG2NrUQOr5cj4DSd3DDIN4wxLi9kXvIAPeejy9AWdjCih\nISOf/Z5y8HJi0zO//XtCpqBrR1U+P4hLHq6UqYn/acodXiLA69rr+wlVyrRBr3+5\nWx5324/0UsqdSixBaUklKhrOi6egUZq05nHUTPaRYsD1FXYAWYJcEtvAOVCNGX1e\n4XFNhpRVbn1cNB/16eLG4cSuca3vGSDnRZCELw9H41YtzunZtO7IANXFXCF23B9I\nW6X4u5hXyfiVELx5amrkFSCMipdrWqeLJJPqsTakn/JnPLaIJzVNAIxxbctTdc12\nH0zlwEH52ur+TGv6bwO+\n=BYun\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T09:43:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDk5NWJiYjc0YWVhN2Q0MzYzNDAzMDE5ZmM1NjQ1NTEzYjI1ODBiZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103","sha":"06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103"}],"sha":"995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/995bbb74aea7d4363403019fc5645513b2580bd4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:26:42Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:45:13Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15202: Migrate sonarqube-scanner to v5\n\n## What\n- Bump sonarqube-scanner from ^3.3.0 to ^5.0.1 in the root project and\n  in the workbench, shared-components and legacy-workbench packages, and\n  adapt the sonar-project.js scripts to the new API.\n- Fix the Sonar source exclusions.\n- Fetch the PR target branch before the Sonar analysis.\n\n## Why\n- The 3.x scanner is outdated and pulls vulnerable transitive\n  dependencies.\n- The exclusion patterns started with ''./'', so they never matched and\n  Sonar indexed fonts and images as sources.\n- The PR checkout contains only the source branch, so Sonar could not\n  find ''master'' and detect the changed lines. It reported issues from\n  unchanged code as new and failed the Quality Gate.\n\n## How\n- v5 is published as an ES module, so require() returns the module\n  namespace instead of a function. The scripts call the named `scan`\n  export and set a non-zero exit code when the analysis fails, instead\n  of ignoring the error in the callback.\n- Drop the ''./'' prefix from the exclusion patterns, since Sonar matches\n  them against paths relative to the base dir, and exclude the remaining\n  image and font directories.\n- Fetch the target branch into refs/remotes/origin for PR builds, inside\n  the existing try/catch, so a failed fetch does not fail the build.\n\n## Testing\nVerified in CI on this PR: the analysis succeeds with scanner 5.0.1,\nSonar finds the merge base with master, skips the excluded directories\nand the Quality Gate passes with 0 new issues.","tree":{"sha":"a576033a39ea69ac01cb0582a9e1624afe69bbbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/a576033a39ea69ac01cb0582a9e1624afe69bbbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72871803?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yordanalexandrov","id":72871803,"login":"yordanalexandrov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyODcxODAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yordanalexandrov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103","node_id":"C_kwDOC73NI9oAKDA2ZDFmMjhkNWM4MzBhNDc4YzUwZmM3MWNlNjIwZmJmYWZmZGIxMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commit/271976e8ed5f28638587db9a1bacee495076d7b0","sha":"271976e8ed5f28638587db9a1bacee495076d7b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/271976e8ed5f28638587db9a1bacee495076d7b0"}],"sha":"06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/06d1f28d5c830a478c50fc71ce620fbfaffdb103"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/commits/271976e8ed5f28638587db9a1bacee495076d7b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:28:38Z","email":"yordan.alexandrov@graphwise.ai","name":"Yordan Alexandrov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:42:16Z","email":"72871803+yordanalexandrov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YAlexandrov"},"message":"GDB-15253: Bump graphwise-styleguide to 1.3.1\n\n## What\nBump graphwise-styleguide from 1.3.0 to 1.3.1 in root-config.\n\n## Why\nThe alert and warning colors were fixed on the workbench side by renaming the --gw-message-warning-* variables to --gw-message-warn-*, while the designer renamed the same tokens in the styleguide itself. That fix is reverted, and this bump takes the styleguide release that defines the --gw-message-warning-* tokens used in common.css.\n\n## How\nUpdate the dependency version in package.json and regenerate package-lock.json.","tree":{"sha":"9890f63f7ffaa9a30b299416132bdcedb68d1b3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/trees/9890f63f7ffaa9a30b299416132bdcedb68d1b3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ontotext-AD/graphdb-workbench/git/commits/271976e8ed5f28638587db9a1bacee495076d7b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/