"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10326572?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leomp12","id":10326572,"login":"leomp12","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzI2NTcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leomp12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ecomplus/storefront/commit/318d6bc91e619b2328ab263019a4b4e7fddfc2b5","node_id":"C_kwDOC_vXMdoAKDMxOGQ2YmM5MWU2MTliMjMyOGFiMjYzMDE5YTRiNGU3ZmRkZmMyYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ecomplus/storefront/commit/96b9b0bf6c5bbe7fe3c1ae7b267e3fdc8dc85d30","sha":"96b9b0bf6c5bbe7fe3c1ae7b267e3fdc8dc85d30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ecomplus/storefront/commits/96b9b0bf6c5bbe7fe3c1ae7b267e3fdc8dc85d30"}],"sha":"318d6bc91e619b2328ab263019a4b4e7fddfc2b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ecomplus/storefront/commits/318d6bc91e619b2328ab263019a4b4e7fddfc2b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35348281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vitorrgg","id":35348281,"login":"vitorrgg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MzQ4Mjgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorrgg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ecomplus/storefront/commits/96b9b0bf6c5bbe7fe3c1ae7b267e3fdc8dc85d30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:18:56Z","email":"35348281+vitorrgg@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vitor Rocha Gonçalves"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:18:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app/account): retry `fetchCustomer` on passport `login` event\n\nReplaces the fixed 1500ms retry with one triggered by the `ecomPassport`\n`login` event, keeping a 3s timer as fallback so the promise always\nsettles. The old timeout could fire before the renewed token reached the\npassport, wasting the single retry and logging the customer out.\n\nOnly 401 takes the event path; other errors keep the previous 1500ms\nretry. `doRetry` checks `checkAuthorization()` on the event path and\nkeeps waiting when the session can''t request the API yet — `login` is\nalso emitted for identified but unauthorized sessions. The fallback timer\nruns unconditionally, so an unauthorized session can never hang it.\n\nRetries right away when the access token changed while the request was in\nflight, since the `login` event is already gone in that case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aeaa102bc490f596dee2f2edea606f99ac65235f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ecomplus/storefront/git/trees/aeaa102bc490f596dee2f2edea606f99ac65235f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ecomplus/storefront/git/commits/96b9b0bf6c5bbe7fe3c1ae7b267e3fdc8dc85d30","verification":{"payload":"tree aeaa102bc490f596dee2f2edea606f99ac65235f\nparent 251fb6fe25d2b5b97f6770240bf39d941243fa7d\nauthor Vitor Rocha Gonçalves <35348281+vitorrgg@users.noreply.github.com> 1785536336 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785536336 -0300\n\nfix(app/account): retry `fetchCustomer` on passport `login` event\n\nReplaces the fixed 1500ms retry with one triggered by the `ecomPassport`\n`login` event, keeping a 3s timer as fallback so the promise always\nsettles. The old timeout could fire before the renewed token reached the\npassport, wasting the single retry and logging the customer out.\n\nOnly 401 takes the event path; other errors keep the previous 1500ms\nretry. `doRetry` checks `checkAuthorization()` on the event path and\nkeeps waiting when the session can''t request the API yet — `login` is\nalso emitted for identified but unauthorized sessions. The fallback timer\nruns unconditionally, so an unauthorized session can never hang it.\n\nRetries right away when the access token changed while the request was in\nflight, since the `login` event is already gone in that case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbR9QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARmQQAKhiUvqetdqCbVY0Te88L4Db\nsyeuSK75Cf5BigioKtC7Vi6+TGFPofjMXfISN7xRAduJeT7Y5O0DyIoezll/zMJ+\nUK4QAjJG5ITXIVrICNEGVGQn3oiItVL6v0kuvk0IIAuKYKj14XO/eaPILZ7OGZ6S\n4gmbfLvIrnRgrtPS76M22NJNqWf4AUHcM2ZR643t3YjjXlyI8jNxjRaSvyjgVofJ\nmQJu9L6I6WN1y4yswbwovEPXDddizCIK6LFT01+4A0pTsSXT8FlJtE/DMlZL4dGg\nzlmgIf63WGp0EnrW7fKHp5I34t34JlbTD5w0TUouNsXcdF3AG8rS0JjbBnPPWwWG\n7LesV3WX1beg8t1AV75NrU2GQo/9t3e/JE3RmuS5n+AYQvbrRg+3aN46nKTz7Q4F\nPtdp9iL2NLVjTYkzpXXTr6EOLapbvQyb7UzUQg31Jnd4tQzXgExGiVm1JrdsKiMf\nUcn9532BDkIm95+xyxn1xdvPDQsCOB2cOc8mIE5yhXR8AudPuzKAfxHpV6J/Cn51\neGYs7/CKybiZsnBf75Z7Zx8lzpVlTlvOvgF9BtRvIXIdi772dHqKQMBeBKpMQGCP\nlS9MeCa8ak4EJCC9CuWZOqSAupCQ2eA