df439144933d2a0658a6008ab111d5327d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1819009?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/loicmathieu","id":1819009,"login":"loicmathieu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTkwMDk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/e0279b03be99e62228763f9b7cb30be86c38b410/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:01:38Z","email":"loikeseke@gmail.com","name":"Loïc Mathieu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:01:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge commit from fork\n\nAuthenticationFilter compared the request path with the literal /api/v1\nprefix and let the request through unauthenticated when it did not match.\nMicronaut prepends the context path to every route, so under a context\npath such as /kestra the whole API was reachable without credentials.\n\nThe context path is now removed, on a segment boundary, from both the raw\nand the decoded path before every prefix and exact-match check.\n\nTenantAliasingRooter had the same blind spot and never aliased tenant-less\nURLs under a context path; it now strips and restores the context path.","tree":{"sha":"638a01470cec4318a5a99375ebe1daed1427f13a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/638a01470cec4318a5a99375ebe1daed1427f13a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/e0279b03be99e62228763f9b7cb30be86c38b410","verification":{"payload":"tree 638a01470cec4318a5a99375ebe1daed1427f13a\nparent 1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b\nauthor Loïc Mathieu <loikeseke@gmail.com> 1791208898 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791208898 +0200\n\nMerge commit from fork\n\nAuthenticationFilter compared the request path with the literal /api/v1\nprefix and let the request through unauthenticated when it did not match.\nMicronaut prepends the context path to every route, so under a context\npath such as /kestra the whole API was reachable without credentials.\n\nThe context path is now removed, on a segment boundary, from both the raw\nand the decoded path before every prefix and exact-match check.\n\nTenantAliasingRooter had the same blind spot and never aliased tenant-less\nURLs under a context path; it now strips and restores the context path.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw63CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYhYQACFhrNphiYhZCHKfT6Dffb80\nTNj5ItvN74m5TDPm5wfwHneN+lk2zNvk4MB5dCJf/FVgBDADBOoHLTnI7tqpqUZA\nVq/Z8AkKdLCgX2I7DXFzebTJPPUwFgfyV7XO6wkdtmEw1xigK+qiSbB6dWYuoAdU\nKXy8burlss/3Fqc8rPcADF7ZEoJ6xzVxOA24acbYKM28GVnPvlfZw/qcjWjrQq1Y\nddxxe/o8g+mpxRmVaIyILxGgDRtb+TO96QYtyi3y9uBcSPibUmrpo5yLSKxaPOMe\nPL/YA2Vgczpd3gRHFWU1p/z63Y3rOg70jfOzmilwkltEZp4cTc/FNZecptGG0Qbd\ntH/kGCS0K4jda5ktbl67bRhDJ1FGbVVxD4RcwN34UVcv99cABjcPM7DKq8cFZINo\n4G+CxqVuGZeoipcLB/5zDDhSwP7zfcPbhhSeGQKfQtFK2yU6wqBORDZPYo/+rim9\nZ+vRTSOVdoZ5d2rGah8luiydM2drXtTi6TprxLto8nmxKCFIYr/arBF8RW7jryJQ\nvDyqmEC3Lpnscs4aQghU3Ffm4jgJD26w2xqpchtvKWHfXuZn+QEnpy5fcYy5WKfr\n2wjyL4OVerN4gw88NxpdqpOu89RQyc8ExhYi8HyqUDOkijlZyv/Gxfukvwwcp41Y\nUhH8MLuV7QVwUAxtNup2\n=M11s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T14:01:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/e0279b03be99e62228763f9b7cb30be86c38b410","node_id":"C_kwDODCtNAdoAKGUwMjc5YjAzYmU5OWU2MjIyODc2M2Y5YjdjYjMwYmU4NmMzOGI0MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b","sha":"1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b"}],"sha":"e0279b03be99e62228763f9b7cb30be86c38b410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/e0279b03be99e62228763f9b7cb30be86c38b410"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1819009?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/loicmathieu","id":1819009,"login":"loicmathieu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTkwMDk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/loicmathieu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:01:14Z","email":"loikeseke@gmail.com","name":"Loïc Mathieu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:01:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge commit from fork\n\nThe denied-list matched the URI text only, so a hostname resolving to a\ndenied IP or CIDR range (an internal DNS name, a wildcard DNS name such\nas 169.254.169.254.sslip.io) was connected to.\n\nInstall a DnsResolver that checks every address a hostname resolves to\nand returns those same addresses to the connection layer, so the name\ncannot resolve to something else after the check. Behind a proxy, which\nresolves the target itself, resolve the host once to check it. IP\nliterals stay with the existing URI check.\n\nAlso strip an IPv6 zone id before parsing a literal: an interface name\nsuch as [::1%lo] was rejected by InetAddress.ofLiteral but accepted by\nthe JDK resolver, so it evaded IP and CIDR entries.","tree":{"sha":"0c97d9ae9fec1b678874b36a5ad99d83b7c4ff02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/0c97d9ae9fec1b678874b36a5ad99d83b7c4ff02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c97d9ae9fec1b678874b36a5ad99d83b7c4ff02\nparent e06b273080b74e08006bad8fe11a4203638fec4e\nauthor Loïc Mathieu <loikeseke@gmail.com> 1791208874 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791208874 +0200\n\nMerge commit from fork\n\nThe denied-list matched the URI text only, so a hostname resolving to a\ndenied IP or CIDR range (an internal DNS name, a wildcard DNS name such\nas 169.254.169.254.sslip.io) was connected to.\n\nInstall a DnsResolver that checks every address a hostname resolves to\nand returns those same addresses to the connection layer, so the name\ncannot resolve to something else after the check. Behind a proxy, which\nresolves the target itself, resolve the host once to check it. IP\nliterals stay with the existing URI check.\n\nAlso strip an IPv6 zone id before parsing a literal: an interface name\nsuch as [::1%lo] was rejected by InetAddress.ofLiteral but accepted by\nthe JDK resolver, so it evaded IP and CIDR entries.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw62qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyUUQAK3VrFy8VsWnzRCrXzk4hOmH\nwONQwJI24fU3A2d1lDQMCio1glMT1j/ynGQR8UK+v7Qm7OiU0QVlDko7hNeIzDBQ\n5dmkprXZjeSXeA6TN67ZpalJUapolRIKluUXkUxCbpByCQMQSJG7Hv+aICwA/PJp\nSWli8i7Gt058J7q3ePE0dR2b9BBmzA9mg6rESydR07qheXNGZBL5tLLW2x1qJlot\nisMBQMoW+AJC4qztOY4/EZz9fOwa8ooqV/JOhed4ixK+zUTwnS+r6z4O5b6fX3zk\nB1sjoG6v60SkiQWVmC5rQGB+tj29JLmJu4oDWZwfJAUSVpGRhfVfe8FUpI1PnIsy\nQPMyxFEYQ8NPqdf/TcTd8XkABQhwEIQ2dYJVyNg9HLDrEKPdYuqNkzzYLofO/A8V\nNcuf/g2ToXOPvZfOiGgvlAp+9CGHCg67j5Psa3pKsdgeHvELPCRXlKTEOQt7geOB\nqs34AGtqaJmlf8PYYzRFdZ44gbxVAnhsFHckDA79PrQigc05xBFvGX3r2LDyLfYR\n/l8BKDyOUB0vkJcINhEGg2+GhCDxLgtMuDE+Cll5so6/Z7MYJzIvHs0YqkCl8kQY\nzrlN/nN8Blie5ttMuH5w14o3HFUPoySkzRLeOu4BygbwwZoHc83PZXTLOehG1Ko4\nlHfzNonpw6NhSruBcqcH\n=8KS0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T14:01:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b","node_id":"C_kwDODCtNAdoAKDFmZTBlOTVjYjU0MjExMDEwM2FjM2VkMWQwMDZiYWQ5MjRhNmFlN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/e06b273080b74e08006bad8fe11a4203638fec4e","sha":"e06b273080b74e08006bad8fe11a4203638fec4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/e06b273080b74e08006bad8fe11a4203638fec4e"}],"sha":"1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/1fe0e95cb542110103ac3ed1d006bad924a6ae7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15046814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AcevedoR","id":15046814,"login":"AcevedoR","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDQ2ODE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/e06b273080b74e08006bad8fe11a4203638fec4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:56:10Z","email":"racevedo@kestra.io","name":"Roman Acevedo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:56:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(triggers): log an unrenderable Flow trigger `when` on both the execution and the flow (#19913)\n\n* fix(triggers): log an unrenderable Flow trigger `when` on both the execution and the flow\n\nA Flow trigger `when` that could not be rendered was treated as a non-match, so the\ntrigger silently never fired — the only trace was a WARN on the upstream execution''s\nlog, and nothing at all on the flow that owns the trigger. The failure is now logged in\nboth places, since the two flows may belong to different teams: a WARN on the evaluated\nexecution (not its error, but it surfaces that something went wrong) and an ERROR on the\nflow that owns the trigger (its own misconfiguration), for both the trigger-level `when`\nand each `dependsOn` entry''s `when`. A `when` that legitimately renders to a falsy value\nstays a silent non-match, and no execution is ever created for an unrenderable one.\n\nAlso exposes `execution.namespace`, `execution.flowId` and `execution.hasRetryAttempt`\non the run context (and documents them), the last replacing the `HasRetryAttempt`\ncondition removed in the 2.0 trigger redesign.\n\nThe executor test harness now wires a real FlowTriggerService, so a full executor cycle\nexercises flow-trigger evaluation end to end.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra-ee/issues/10857\n\n* fix(triggers): address review on the unrenderable `when` fix\n\n- drop execution.namespace/flowId (redundant with flow.namespace/flow.id)\n- replace the misleading execution.hasRetryAttempt with execution.attemptNumber,\n  the execution-level retry count from the metadata\n- spell out ''the downstream flow will not be started'' in both logs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nKwiatkowski <nkwiatkowski@kestra.io>","tree":{"sha":"ad9a310f32891c79b9cdff55a2428633519a0986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/ad9a310f32891c79b9cdff55a2428633519a0986"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/e06b273080b74e08006bad8fe11a4203638fec4e","verification":{"payload":"tree ad9a310f32891c79b9cdff55a2428633519a0986\nparent 799c58ec38d1a120670c761ae8336e3c1ec7f28d\nauthor Roman Acevedo <racevedo@kestra.io> 1791208570 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791208570 +0200\n\nfix(triggers): log an unrenderable Flow trigger `when` on both the execution and the flow (#19913)\n\n* fix(triggers): log an unrenderable Flow trigger `when` on both the execution and the flow\n\nA Flow trigger `when` that could not be rendered was treated as a non-match, so the\ntrigger silently never fired — the only trace was a WARN on the upstream execution''s\nlog, and nothing at all on the flow that owns the trigger. The failure is now logged in\nboth places, since the two flows may belong to different teams: a WARN on the evaluated\nexecution (not its error, but it surfaces that something went wrong) and an ERROR on the\nflow that owns the trigger (its own misconfiguration), for both the trigger-level `when`\nand each `dependsOn` entry''s `when`. A `when` that legitimately renders to a falsy value\nstays a silent non-match, and no execution is ever created for an unrenderable one.\n\nAlso exposes `execution.namespace`, `execution.flowId` and `execution.hasRetryAttempt`\non the run context (and documents them), the last replacing the `HasRetryAttempt`\ncondition removed in the 2.0 trigger redesign.\n\nThe executor test harness now wires a real FlowTriggerService, so a full executor cycle\nexercises flow-trigger evaluation end to end.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra-ee/issues/10857\n\n* fix(triggers): address review on the unrenderable `when` fix\n\n- drop execution.namespace/flowId (redundant with flow.namespace/flow.id)\n- replace the misleading execution.hasRetryAttempt with execution.attemptNumber,\n  the execution-level retry count from the metadata\n- spell out ''the downstream flow will not be started'' in both logs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nKwiatkowski <nkwiatkowski@kestra.io>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6x6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAot8QADxbgHpFAzk4ok/8THXxHy86\nkabtbeJ0+wYtDceNAoMGZ7EBn9Reo2IXDTv9pGK/qilu2Gx2mtTJMLP36RwmZpJC\nbUkC3LSGBsZzzi8NyLkggoJacGaWlX5esZ0wlR6a/oyf5qZNJrfiUcfFTV59WkOj\nBFAp2s7WByeww2oKEAdDg+1e1CsoyxrL8vZHbiWkF0UVa4dtt8GKr0Sgf6LSCi1O\n8ie7WBsSGNDq44fPAeuua8ahyqzAOmw5vKFIx/Nx60QInAG5346hav0Ak9oFkM4+\nm4O9XXgY2e7KpXV6EHmGvYx14eEBtzBXlt7pFZagh11VKxucN8Iu8iMx8YZ3JUP5\niOwNtsZnL1xrefLznLcyzWQdTDmgkuP4mHmNH4HdnByHb2tk6Ye6jdT5aH54WTkY\n3J60XMFyE8dvjXCJKuVwz9ssdt14J74znLl88cpg0m+JdLd6TrplIQB3hJ1uUUkx\nGf541TGeOK9w2vavMbkh5QTYWnCwMPjFBa1/slXTJD13BtHTqX4eK6QJGxQtP+1y\nz/5uQMA2MIiRyzBUMdkaSn/SDkYkkmZHvKLc/CIcNG6tPGWqAOwteMX6H925JgX5\nGJNw+eSjOy40DrMVGeeMpYDQ4ECLDOxgujsJXJ/3DjCo4y+TdGN3ibuW5a+HaIBD\nn+t7X+vcNzmT9rHhNaDt\n=EyIt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:56:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"h