_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/9029b83cb03e9bb86bc54db71a0741ee9ba2175b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:50:27Z","email":"roman.acevedo62@gmail.com","name":"Roman Acevedo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:21:53Z","email":"roman.acevedo62@gmail.com","name":"Roman Acevedo"},"message":"fix(executions): bound Subflow retries and keep a killed Subflow killed when its outputs cannot be rendered\n\nWhen the outputs of a subflow could not be rendered, Subflow.failSubflowDueToOutput replaced the attempts of the\nSubflow task run with a single one, so a retry never reached maxAttempts and the parent ran the subflow forever.\nIt also failed the task run whatever the subflow ended in: the kill of a parent cascades to its subflow, the\nkilled subflow came back FAILED, and the retry revived the killed parent. The same happened one level down, as a\nkilled execution whose own outputs cannot be rendered was turned into a FAILED one.\n\nfailSubflowDueToOutput now adds an attempt and keeps KILLED for a killed subflow, and the executor no longer\nfails a killed execution because its outputs cannot be rendered.","tree":{"sha":"53429f6897a55f6251814db324cc69f6a4939906","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/53429f6897a55f6251814db324cc69f6a4939906"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/9029b83cb03e9bb86bc54db71a0741ee9ba2175b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15046814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AcevedoR","id":15046814,"login":"AcevedoR","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDQ2ODE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/9029b83cb03e9bb86bc54db71a0741ee9ba2175b","node_id":"C_kwDODCtNAdoAKDkwMjliODNjYjAzZTliYjg2YmM1NGRiNzFhMDc0MWVlOWJhMjE3NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b","sha":"dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b"}],"sha":"9029b83cb03e9bb86bc54db71a0741ee9ba2175b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/9029b83cb03e9bb86bc54db71a0741ee9ba2175b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97828805?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/deveshpandee","id":97828805,"login":"deveshpandee","node_id":"U_kgDOBdS_xQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deveshpandee","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:20:57Z","email":"97828805+deveshpandee@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Devesh Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:20:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(flows): add unit tests for useStoredPanels (#20262)\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/issues/20196.\n\nuseStoredPanels persists the editor panel layout and its serializer\ndeliberately drops tabs that no longer deserialize. Cover the round\ntrip and the degradation paths so a reviewer learns from a failure:\nserialization shape, restore via deserialize callbacks, a dropped tab\nwhose panel survives, an empty stored panel being removed, active-tab\nfallback, the keyless plain-ref path, and saveState under an alternate\nkey.","tree":{"sha":"acf7eac475452361c713bd5af58b52cfb8851d01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/acf7eac475452361c713bd5af58b52cfb8851d01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b","verification":{"payload":"tree acf7eac475452361c713bd5af58b52cfb8851d01\nparent 65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf\nauthor Devesh Kumar <97828805+deveshpandee@users.noreply.github.com> 1791206457 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791206457 +0200\n\ntest(flows): add unit tests for useStoredPanels (#20262)\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/issues/20196.\n\nuseStoredPanels persists the editor panel layout and its serializer\ndeliberately drops tabs that no longer deserialize. Cover the round\ntrip and the degradation paths so a reviewer learns from a failure:\nserialization shape, restore via deserialize callbacks, a dropped tab\nwhose panel survives, an empty stored panel being removed, active-tab\nfallback, the keyless plain-ref path, and saveState under an alternate\nkey.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6Q5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAksMQABj20bysE7h4xNMUVTarzKTS\nOZuJBJ5QWFJU+tOQOTKyuMZl8ntct6TGprGmIPEtgZ+bTNF+DVDG+suWKuut82vT\n11vFiSBkVJYjzRvNUhfczHr7bqMFGdO6GR1dwQqFy2Z/7L6ABP5DO3mrh2GLq/EH\nmZLqe/isENCniBDPb6xpTGgLpia9WfqtgcSFEecCbsXk2PdrzUF+D1mD8WZyY4nO\nls17JiMMjLGeycSehJEggoqcUl9opW1PoqjW8ufywks/mkfiKbCAL2PzGVagyPtW\niiTay6QQpiJFSJADNTNx5kaPBmE12Umv8pTsCqPPAkGe858TZaYFHbSr5bxkXnfp\niw3IWnsf6X4EYt1mL6ya3jdTILStPy6fF703henWrItEh531Gs47dI9y45WNwYBM\nXav9nxNF/j8QP5taewpgnvSzBZkKDMhG5kGH01gPDvwjiwNRNDoSurOQ1FMNbYmv\n+vPDsLLu6pQhgoRkAbZGhzhgYmxBZRP3fgXhLpAzyygV852e1LngZT+KNXQ+PTA3\nzcO5nEsiMCmD4DjOr99OurUDefJmMX40CRKqQHs4sQPej5K4Z0CwRZghlqpg/sIO\nh9PP/zgHapT5i1EQpbqoVA4xPk2OCszpLxYhN9yLk3cvJLGZjROVr7tkfVMpHeWo\nvy2PzdbQDNcJb6CbUFuT\n=O2Lk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:20:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b","node_id":"C_kwDODCtNAdoAKGRkOTg3MDk0N2M1ZjhlMGFiOTFmZGU1NTcyYzQzZmIwNjVmNWU4MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf","sha":"65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf"}],"sha":"dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/dd9870947c5f8e0ab91fde5572c43fb065f5e80b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5592465?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elevatebart","id":5592465,"login":"elevatebart","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1OTI0NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:41:12Z","email":"bledoux@kestra.io","name":"Barthélémy Ledoux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:41:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(flows): show backend validation errors as Monaco markers (#20013)\n\n* feat(flows): locate backend validation errors in the code editor\n\n/flows/validate now returns each violation with an RFC 6901 pointer next to\nthe flat constraints string. The editor resolves pointers against the YAML\nAST: unknown keys get squiggled on the key, missing keys on the enclosing\nblock. Jackson''s reference chain no longer masquerades as a property path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): report unknown and missing properties in one validation pass\n\nThe strict parse bailed at the first unknown key, so a stray `colour:` hid\nevery missing `message:` behind it. Unknown keys are now collected by\nremoving each one and re-parsing, then bean validation runs as usual.\n\nAlso fixes ViolationPaths.toJsonPointer: Micronaut puts a list index on the\nnode after the collection, which produced /tasks/tasks/0/message/1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): keep validating past an unknown plugin type\n\nA task with an unresolvable `type` aborted the whole validation, hiding\nevery other squiggle in the flow. The scan now drops that plugin, maps\nlater error paths back over the removed index, and swallows the errors\nthe removal itself causes (an emptied `tasks` list). Auto-installable\nplugins stay notices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): squiggle only the text of a block, one line at a time\n\nA multi-line marker underlined the indentation and trailing comments of\nevery line it crossed. Block markers are now split per line and span the\nfirst to the last key or value on it. Adds a story per violation kind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): name the property in located bean-validation messages\n\nA missing-key marker sits on the enclosing block, so \"must not be null\"\nalone left the reader guessing which key. It now reads \"message: must not\nbe null\". Jackson-side messages already name their key and are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* feat(flows): report validation errors as RFC 9457 errors entries\n\nValidation results now carry `errors`, one ValidationError per problem\nwith the same detail/pointer/path members as a problem document''s\n`errors`, so the UI stops splitting the `constraints` string. Producers\nthat only set `constraints` (the EE validators) still expose one entry per\nline through the getter; `constraints` itself is deprecated, not removed.\n\nThe editor names the missing key itself, which drops the backend prefix.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/issues/18972.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): group no-code validation issues by pointer\n\ngroupValidationIssuesByTask walked the error text with two regexes to\nguess which task a line belonged to. It now walks each error''s pointer\nthrough the parsed flow and files it under the deepest task it crosses,\nthe rest of the pointer naming the field.\n\nPointers name Java properties, so `/_finally/...` falls back to the YAML\nkey `finally`; before this, a finally task got neither a squiggle nor a\nbadge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): address review on validation markers and parsing cost\n\n- Missing-key markers stay on the block''s own keys and values: visit()\n  descended into nested tasks, so an If missing `condition` underlined\n  its whole `then` branch.\n- The strict parse is the fast path again; only a source it rejects is\n  scanned, so a valid flow is parsed once per validate.\n- A valid result reports `errors: []` rather than null, like the other\n  lists on the DTO.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): move the Monaco markers to their own stacked PR\n\nThis PR now carries the RFC 9457 `errors` report and the UI that reads\nit; the editor squiggles are reviewed separately on top of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* feat(flows): show backend validation errors as Monaco markers\n\nResolves each RFC 9457 `errors` pointer against the YAML AST and marks it\nin the flow code editor: an unknown key on the key and its value, a\nmissing key on its enclosing block line by line (indentation, dashes,\ncomments and nested tasks left alone), an invalid type on `type`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): one marker per violation, block scalar bodies left alone\n\n- A multi-line scalar is marked on its first line, so a `|` script no\n  longer gets squiggled line by line.\n- Each violation is one marker; the rest of its block gets the same\n  squiggle as a decoration, so the Problems list stops repeating itself.\n- The composable clears the model it marked, not whichever the editor\n  holds now.\n- Pointers naming no scalar fall back to the last key on the path, and a\n  duplicate key no longer hides every marker.\n- The story follows its `errors` control.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(core): one list-index check and one path renderer for parse reports\n\n- `ParseReport.isIndex` replaces the NumberFormatException probe in\n  `shift` and the digit checks in `toPath` and `YamlParser.listIndex`.\n- `YamlParser.propertyPath` renders through `ParseReport.toPath`.\n- `/validate/task` pins that an invalid type yields exactly one `errors`\n  entry, so the dedup in `ValidationError.ofException` cannot drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* build(deps): regenerate kestra-sdk with ValidationError\n\nThe UI now types validation results from the SDK, so the local\n`ValidationError` interface and the `{errors?}` casts are gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): markers only for the current flow, plain-text hovers\n\n- Loading a flow clears the previous validation, and an overtaken\n  validation response is dropped, so old pointers never squiggle the new\n  source.\n- Continuation-line hovers escape markdown, matching the marker text.\n- The squiggle decoration lives in an editor-scoped collection, under a\n  named class constant.\n- The same violation reported twice is marked once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* test(flows): type the overtaken-validation spec with the SDK result\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): drop `constraints` from validation results\n\n`errors` is now the only way a validation result reports a problem, so\nthe newline-joined string and the getter that rebuilt `errors` from it\nare gone. Every producer and reader moves to `errors`: FlowService,\nFlowController''s task and trigger validators, the AI validation tools,\nand the flow, blueprint and dashboard stores. An exception without\nviolations still keeps its message as one unlocated error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): escape `&` in the violation hover so entities stay verbatim\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): drop the self-evident `errors` schema description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): keep `constraints` as a deprecated view of `errors`\n\nOne line per error, so API consumers reading the old string keep working.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): keep the scan''s state inside ParseReport and report every stopping error\n\nA value error after an unknown key used to drop both behind one /yaml error. The scan now\nlocates each problem and removes it, and FlowService only reads errors, types and the\nrecovered source.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): keep the Lombok builder out of a method signature so javadoc builds\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9f580c8d033c88d9720fa3194204e673d23e961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/a9f580c8d033c88d9720fa3194204e673d23e961"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf","verification":{"payload":"tree a9f580c8d033c88d9720fa3194204e673d23e961\nparent 1fde660701051aee3b353f57a635f8567b8c2cb4\nauthor Barthélémy Ledoux <bledoux@kestra.io> 1791204072 +0200\ncom