7b8c2cb4"}],"sha":"65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/65f74305d0d242d8fe8fe04b0b9207581f1b9caf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5592465?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elevatebart","id":5592465,"login":"elevatebart","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1OTI0NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/1fde660701051aee3b353f57a635f8567b8c2cb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:32:57Z","email":"bledoux@kestra.io","name":"Barthélémy Ledoux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:32:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(flows): report validation errors as RFC 9457 errors entries (#19999)\n\n* feat(flows): locate backend validation errors in the code editor\n\n/flows/validate now returns each violation with an RFC 6901 pointer next to\nthe flat constraints string. The editor resolves pointers against the YAML\nAST: unknown keys get squiggled on the key, missing keys on the enclosing\nblock. Jackson''s reference chain no longer masquerades as a property path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): report unknown and missing properties in one validation pass\n\nThe strict parse bailed at the first unknown key, so a stray `colour:` hid\nevery missing `message:` behind it. Unknown keys are now collected by\nremoving each one and re-parsing, then bean validation runs as usual.\n\nAlso fixes ViolationPaths.toJsonPointer: Micronaut puts a list index on the\nnode after the collection, which produced /tasks/tasks/0/message/1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): keep validating past an unknown plugin type\n\nA task with an unresolvable `type` aborted the whole validation, hiding\nevery other squiggle in the flow. The scan now drops that plugin, maps\nlater error paths back over the removed index, and swallows the errors\nthe removal itself causes (an emptied `tasks` list). Auto-installable\nplugins stay notices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): squiggle only the text of a block, one line at a time\n\nA multi-line marker underlined the indentation and trailing comments of\nevery line it crossed. Block markers are now split per line and span the\nfirst to the last key or value on it. Adds a story per violation kind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): name the property in located bean-validation messages\n\nA missing-key marker sits on the enclosing block, so \"must not be null\"\nalone left the reader guessing which key. It now reads \"message: must not\nbe null\". Jackson-side messages already name their key and are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* feat(flows): report validation errors as RFC 9457 errors entries\n\nValidation results now carry `errors`, one ValidationError per problem\nwith the same detail/pointer/path members as a problem document''s\n`errors`, so the UI stops splitting the `constraints` string. Producers\nthat only set `constraints` (the EE validators) still expose one entry per\nline through the getter; `constraints` itself is deprecated, not removed.\n\nThe editor names the missing key itself, which drops the backend prefix.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/issues/18972.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): group no-code validation issues by pointer\n\ngroupValidationIssuesByTask walked the error text with two regexes to\nguess which task a line belonged to. It now walks each error''s pointer\nthrough the parsed flow and files it under the deepest task it crosses,\nthe rest of the pointer naming the field.\n\nPointers name Java properties, so `/_finally/...` falls back to the YAML\nkey `finally`; before this, a finally task got neither a squiggle nor a\nbadge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): address review on validation markers and parsing cost\n\n- Missing-key markers stay on the block''s own keys and values: visit()\n  descended into nested tasks, so an If missing `condition` underlined\n  its whole `then` branch.\n- The strict parse is the fast path again; only a source it rejects is\n  scanned, so a valid flow is parsed once per validate.\n- A valid result reports `errors: []` rather than null, like the other\n  lists on the DTO.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): move the Monaco markers to their own stacked PR\n\nThis PR now carries the RFC 9457 `errors` report and the UI that reads\nit; the editor squiggles are reviewed separately on top of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(core): one list-index check and one path renderer for parse reports\n\n- `ParseReport.isIndex` replaces the NumberFormatException probe in\n  `shift` and the digit checks in `toPath` and `YamlParser.listIndex`.\n- `YamlParser.propertyPath` renders through `ParseReport.toPath`.\n- `/validate/task` pins that an invalid type yields exactly one `errors`\n  entry, so the dedup in `ValidationError.ofException` cannot drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* build(deps): regenerate kestra-sdk with ValidationError\n\nThe UI now types validation results from the SDK, so the local\n`ValidationError` interface and the `{errors?}` casts are gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): drop `constraints` from validation results\n\n`errors` is now the only way a validation result reports a problem, so\nthe newline-joined string and the getter that rebuilt `errors` from it\nare gone. Every producer and reader moves to `errors`: FlowService,\nFlowController''s task and trigger validators, the AI validation tools,\nand the flow, blueprint and dashboard stores. An exception without\nviolations still keeps its message as one unlocated error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): drop the self-evident `errors` schema description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): keep `constraints` as a deprecated view of `errors`\n\nOne line per error, so API consumers reading the old string keep working.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): keep the scan''s state inside ParseReport and report every stopping error\n\nA value error after an unknown key used to drop both behind one /yaml error. The scan now\nlocates each problem and removes it, and FlowService only reads errors, types and the\nrecovered source.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): keep the Lombok builder out of a method signature so javadoc builds\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c71bcac967ce853d3d976ca5a18e19a23bbd1937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/c71bcac967ce853d3d976ca5a18e19a23bbd1937"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/1fde660701051aee3b353f57a635f8567b8c2cb4","verification":{"payload":"tree c71bcac967ce853d3d976ca5a18e19a23bbd1937\nparent 8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba\nauthor Barthélémy Ledoux <bledoux@kestra.io> 1791203577 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791203577 +0200\n\nfeat(flows): report validation errors as RFC 9457 errors entries (#19999)\n\n* feat(flows): locate backend validation errors in the code editor\n\n/flows/validate now returns each violation with an RFC 6901 pointer next to\nthe flat constraints string. The editor resolves pointers against the YAML\nAST: unknown keys get squiggled on the key, missing keys on the enclosing\nblock. Jackson''s reference chain no longer masquerades as a property path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): report unknown and missing properties in one validation pass\n\nThe strict parse bailed at the first unknown key, so a stray `colour:` hid\nevery missing `message:` behind it. Unknown keys are now collected by\nremoving each one and re-parsing, then bean validation runs as usual.\n\nAlso fixes ViolationPaths.toJsonPointer: Micronaut puts a list index on the\nnode after the collection, which produced /tasks/tasks/0/message/1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): keep validating past an unknown plugin type\n\nA task with an unresolvable `type` aborted the whole validation, hiding\nevery other squiggle in the flow. The scan now drops that plugin, maps\nlater error paths back over the removed index, and swallows the errors\nthe removal itself causes (an emptied `tasks` list). Auto-installable\nplugins stay notices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): squiggle only the text of a block, one line at a time\n\nA multi-line marker underlined the indentation and trailing comments of\nevery line it crossed. Block markers are now split per line and span the\nfirst to the last key or value on it. Adds a story per violation kind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): name the property in located bean-validation messages\n\nA missing-key marker sits on the enclosing block, so \"must not be null\"\nalone left the reader guessing which key. It now reads \"message: must not\nbe null\". Jackson-side messages already name their key and are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* feat(flows): report validation errors as RFC 9457 errors entries\n\nValidation results now carry `errors`, one ValidationError per problem\nwith the same detail/pointer/path members as a problem document''s\n`errors`, so the UI stops splitting the `constraints` string. Producers\nthat only set `constraints` (the EE validators) still expose one entry per\nline through the getter; `constraints` itself is deprecated, not removed.\n\nThe editor names the missing key itself, which drops the backend prefix.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/issues/18972.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): group no-code validation issues by pointer\n\ngroupValidationIssuesByTask walked the error text with two regexes to\nguess which task a line belonged to. It now walks each error''s pointer\nthrough the parsed flow and files it under the deepest task it crosses,\nthe rest of the pointer naming the field.\n\nPointers name Java properties, so `/_finally/...` falls back to the YAML\nkey `finally`; before this, a finally task got neither a squiggle nor a\nbadge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): address review on validation markers and parsing cost\n\n- Missing-key markers stay on the block''s own keys and values: visit()\n  descended into nested tasks, so an If missing `condition` underlined\n  its whole `then` branch.\n- The strict parse is the fast path again; only a source it rejects is\n  scanned, so a valid flow is parsed once per validate.\n- A valid result reports `errors: []` rather than null, like the other\n  lists on the DTO.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): move the Monaco markers to their own stacked PR\n\nThis PR now carries the RFC 9457 `errors` report and the UI that reads\nit; the editor squiggles are reviewed separately on top of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(core): one list-index check and one path renderer for parse reports\n\n- `ParseReport.isIndex` replaces the NumberFormatException probe in\n  `shift` and the digit checks in `toPath` and `YamlParser.listIndex`.\n- `YamlParser.propertyPath` renders through `ParseReport.toPath`.\n- `/validate/task` pins that an invalid type yields exactly one `errors`\n  entry, so the dedup in `ValidationError.ofException` cannot drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* build(deps): regenerate kestra-sdk with ValidationError\n\nThe UI now types validation results from the SDK, so the local\n`ValidationError` interface and the `{errors?}` casts are gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): drop `constraints` from validation results\n\n`errors` is now the only way a validation result reports a problem, so\nthe newline-joined string and the getter that rebuilt `errors` from it\nare gone. Every producer and reader moves to `errors`: FlowService,\nFlowController''s task and trigger validators, the AI validation tools,\nand the flow, blueprint and dashboard stores. An exception without\nviolations still keeps its message as one unlocated error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): drop the self-evident `errors` schema description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): keep `constraints` as a deprecated view of `errors`\n\nOne line per error, so API consumers reading the old string keep working.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* refactor(flows): keep the scan''s state inside ParseReport and report every stopping error\n\nA value error after an unknown key used to drop both behind one /yaml error. The scan now\nlocates each problem and removes it, and FlowService only reads errors, types and the\nrecovered source.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n* fix(flows): keep the Lombok builder out of a method signature so javadoc builds\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018URtsoowN7VwLe6BUr9zp8\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw5j5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz+wQAFVKP0YkIDScIpYsE/RLzGRR\n8RFFCZeSK/1jO80EOgQ0PoZxI6MmLKzuYw0N6Xlvi3O6l4zilYajcNKTQkivRqrv\nrB5MVdIvbLOuoB0p2Xxwanf/5hv4p4dxO5iMQbDEz5m9Ei8L0dny8Vxd1Pj4ipS/\nyQIShVdPXwKd3A5McgDiaYMhanC2lHuXPytaTqOzDawO58fPN1//TW+ycrd8U76G\nisMVREMY26vRbNLBBQXvmsqa3jyXSX9dHv8JX8ChyJigo8V2eOlm1lq24MGi5oRZ\nhpgflpF9JWPrgqhdF9iwPsVHSDgIkP7ba0ffDxcmGb8AJF3AJvSqf6AzJRnPctHU\nlDQhd7vIf88gwVFnK7vXcNhiiqt+SLffLDuJUH8CaFNS91QC9UMI9QV7mgLoiWb3\nkcVZWKQMQMgt/aHqlcVQI4HFnxh9RXr7iko9nDnIma2uxs3f6ZSQybU3VRJW+ut+\nxX6FBM/Fkm7Ybn9/DPnyZoFy+6gc+bPvHd2RI2kMLfYxS8x5O3IhfDonaEhN8166\n4WVmL/fjG/coJhxNT7vifXG6JFfnQfYTbrCGR+xrl6aQMWx+EmYFAMS6/4sxElpY\nBBeiNGu/YF8nWILnpJNqh4kRs/3U7vw+MyGn83h1GsXvT1W+UrTmhvZTwp1GhpCv\nhAxjXvkWDz+V5ON659yA\n=QFyh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T12:32:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/1fde660701051aee3b353f57a635f8567b8c2cb4","node_id":"C_kwDODCtNAdoAKDFmZGU2NjA3MDEwNTFhZWUzYjM1M2Y1N2E2MzVmODU2N2I4YzJjYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba","sha":"8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba"}],"sha":"1fde660701051aee3b353f57a635f8567b8c2cb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/1fde660701051aee3b353f57a635f8567b8c2cb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15046814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AcevedoR","id":15046814,"login":"AcevedoR","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDQ2ODE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:49:05Z","email":"roman.acevedo62@gmail.com","name":"Roman Acevedo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:31:26Z","email":"roman.acevedo62@gmail.com","name":"Roman Acevedo"},"message":"fix(system): seed pip into the kestra-base python venv\n\nThe venv was created without pip, so pip resolved to the system /usr/bin/pip,\nwhich Ubuntu 24.04 refuses to use (PEP 668, externally-managed-environment).\nPython script tasks with pip install in beforeCommands failed on every image\nbuilt from the python kestra-base variants.","tree":{"sha":"2402f3a3a158545e747c6a4366781a84f3d8a602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/2402f3a3a158545e747c6a4366781a84f3d8a602"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15046814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AcevedoR","id":15046814,"login":"AcevedoR","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDQ2ODE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AcevedoR","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba","node_id":"C_kwDODCtNAdoAKDhkNDg3MDg5Y2E1OGQ3Y2MzY2Y1ZmI4YWI2ZDlkODFjZDI3Y2E4YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra/commit/a5aa7806b543c7faf6e89d70f20214177b74fd99","sha":"a5aa7806b543c7faf6e89d70f20214177b74fd99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/a5aa7806b543c7faf6e89d70f20214177b74fd99"}],"sha":"8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/8d487089ca58d7cc3cf5fb8ab6d9d81cd27ca8ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5592465?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elevatebart","id":5592465,"login":"elevatebart","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1OTI0NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elevatebart","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/a5aa7806b543c7faf6e89d70f20214177b74fd99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:31:11Z","email":"bledoux@kestra.io","name":"Barthélémy Ledoux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:31:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(flows): playground run task stuck disabled when no execution starts (#20369)\n\n* fix(flows): playground Run task stuck disabled when no execution starts\n\nreadyToStart was a latch flipped off on click and only restored by a\nwatcher that never fires if nothing actually runs (cancelled create\ndialog, rejected trigger). It is now derived from an in-flight flag\nreset in a finally, so the button cannot outlive the request.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra-ee/issues/9724.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012X7H2iEK4GvHrQ7NtJhAFP\n\n* test(flows): pin the playground in-flight guard\n\nAdds the in-flight case so dropping the starting flag goes red, and stops\nwrapping the flow store mock in a reactive proxy that Object.assign\nunwrapped anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012X7H2iEK4GvHrQ7NtJhAFP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"941f2149ac289d3f339c9f4c1c5bf27fe00d8f5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/941f2149ac289d3f339c9f4c1c5bf27fe00d8f5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/a5aa7806b543c7faf6e89d70f20214177b74fd99","verification":{"payload":"tree 941f2149ac289d3f339c9f4c1c5bf27fe00d8f5d\nparent d7869ee2704ab3e6efbd5312a8240da79175208e\nauthor Barthélémy Ledoux <bledoux@kestra.io> 1791203471 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791203471 +0200\n\nfix(flows): playground run task stuck disabled when no execution starts (#20369)\n\n* fix(flows): playground Run task stuck disabled when no execution starts\n\nreadyToStart was a latch flipped off on click and only restored by a\nwatcher that never fires if nothing actually runs (cancelled create\ndialog, rejected trigger). It is now derived from an in-flight flag\nreset in a finally, so the button cannot outlive the request.\n\nCloses https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra-ee/issues/9724.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012X7H2iEK4GvHrQ7NtJhAFP\n\n* test(flows): pin the playground in-flight guard\n\nAdds the in-flight case so dropping the starting flag goes red, and stops\nwrapping the flow store mock in a reactive proxy that Object.assign\nunwrapped anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012X7H2iEK4GvHrQ7NtJhAFP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw5iPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArq4QAFMbrJLlspJhMJOtJqBdf05h\neWRyW2Lxjm2KJWDncuOjubXR2ugb25qQMO0dduLKv2tt4vAe80PV9Z/igPSBJfua\nukIy04VhNOU69lYPVDfiC6L+4WPTajphXnQGyLLAINfcwohSTgv07l+qiiV/0fY0\naGyXsT5xVDNxlGGX8BNXpu+1BQgumUK68TdJxCxasOTyWL6yAkewPIr+ExcitlU3\nw6Kp9+dFPuCyisAEmLx5BdxBBJGdpPciNHxW1XT3ME7DBiQaCRMP+xsS0vFma9b/\na5WIc5lxyqnqySGyUGS5P7ccmxxo66wDGFsBoMjT9OAcGjXgzJZy1IXjozGcWDve\nqimqf2R7jNQD9Oaer/GZoU0u9jHeHDsL9JVeOgQcK90HXyurEhcs5/3c0PbztMzh\nmXgawuIRPKXb7tW/O+kJJH9TgewDAkLztqvg6A6fw3s+bc3TfrJl2i68LoNcrXn2\nvmMirl3U8mjpGeM8fTVYEkMh1D9sM9hAYedM3QILZ/rKAfN0KQ4rN/GVXjm4meX4\nUZKYXMKm8n6qnwcVyFyVIB8R6T8h01KdGCyXMlLNTnq0eILyljzvmjEHkMaZvtql\nPpqQJvY3kpDioW9UpyuEexFxponOv3lZY4BRQ4jLCzgaGKyXawyVRzH8PWfEnsXt\nPFtRulQTUvQqSYYqOSNQ\n=fWbY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T12:31:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/