its/d7869ee2704ab3e6efbd5312a8240da79175208e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20555275?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nkwiatkowski","id":20555275,"login":"nkwiatkowski","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTU1Mjc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nkwiatkowski","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/commits/779c9a490c3f78fe20a9dfc2b9883116160ece94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:05:35Z","email":"nk_mikmak@hotmail.com","name":"Nicolas K."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:05:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plugins): serve plugin-defined HTTP endpoints from core (#19807)\n\n* feat(plugins): serve plugin-defined http endpoints from core\n\nPlugins declare a PluginEndpoint (name + handle) in plain Java, with no\nMicronaut and no access to Kestra internals; the request carries only\nparameters + body and the response is bytes + content-type. Core discovers\nimplementations through the existing plugin ServiceLoader and collects them on\nRegisteredPlugin. A new webserver controller dispatches\nGET|POST /api/v1/{tenant}/plugins/{group}/endpoints/{name} to the matching\nhandler, hardens the response (X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff; application/json\ninline, anything else forced to attachment), and a server filter caps the\nrequest body. First stone for the plugin-endpoint bridge.\n\nRefs https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra-ee/issues/9994\n\n* feat(plugins): scoped execution capabilities for plugin endpoints\n\nA plugin endpoint is now invoked for a specific execution/taskRun and\nreceives, through PluginEndpointContext, read access to that taskRun''s\nlogs and outputs and read/write access to that execution''s internal\nstorage — each scoped by construction to that one execution/taskRun.\n\n- route gains required path vars /endpoints/{name}/{executionId}/{taskRunId}\n- handle(PluginEndpointContext ctx); body is a parsed JSON object (Map),\n  response may name a file (Content-Disposition, sanitized)\n- ScopedStorage confines every URI to the execution storage prefix;\n  logs use the ACL finder; outputs read off the ACL-loaded execution\n- dispatch authorizes the execution (ACL findById + namespace) before\n  resolving the plugin, so an unauthorized caller learns nothing about it\n\n* fix(plugins): address review on scoped plugin endpoints\n\n- read outputs through TaskOutputService (TaskRun.getOutputs() is removed in 2.0)\n- address endpoints by plugin class ({cls}) resolved via RegisteredPlugin.hasClass,\n  which is what the calling task UI holds; endpoints stay plugin-scoped\n- make JSON-only explicit: @Consumes(application/json) + @Body Map<String,Object>\n- ScopedStorage rejects any non-kestra:// URI\n- make the feature toggleable with kestra.plugins.endpoint.enabled (controller not\n  loaded when disabled) and expose it to the UI via /configs\n- make the request-body cap configurable (kestra.plugins.endpoint.max-body-size)\n- rename TaskRunLogs/TaskRunOutputs to ...Fetcher, drop a dead null check\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nKwiatkowski <nkwiatkowski@kestra.io>","tree":{"sha":"1b191023d41870eb6d671162539e088c6e5bda40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/trees/1b191023d41870eb6d671162539e088c6e5bda40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kestra-io/kestra/git/commits/779c9a490c3f78fe20a9dfc2b9883116160ece94","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b191023d41870eb6d671162539e088c6e5bda40\nparent 29f03cfa71bede862ef96d97ca138e4ff533a833\nauthor Nicolas K. <nk_mikmak@hotmail.com> 1791201935 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791201935 +0200\n\nfeat(plugins): serve plugin-defined HTTP endpoints from core (#19807)\n\n* feat(plugins): serve plugin-defined http endpoints from core\n\nPlugins declare a PluginEndpoint (name + handle) in plain Java, with no\nMicronaut and no access to Kestra internals; the request carries only\nparameters + body and the response is bytes + content-type. Core discovers\nimplementations through the existing plugin ServiceLoader and collects them on\nRegisteredPlugin. A new webserver controller dispatches\nGET|POST /api/v1/{tenant}/plugins/{group}/endpoints/{name} to the matching\nhandler, hardens the response (X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff; application/json\ninline, anything else forced to attachment), and a server filter caps the\nrequest body. First stone for the plugin-endpoint bridge.\n\nRefs https://github.com/kestra-io/kestra-ee/issues/9994\n\n* feat(plugins): scoped execution capabilities for plugin endpoints\n\nA plugin endpoint is now invoked for a specific execution/taskRun and\nreceives, through PluginEndpointContext, read access to that taskRun''s\nlogs and outputs and read/write access to that execution''s internal\nstorage — each scoped by construction to that one execution/taskRun.\n\n- route gains required path vars /endpoints/{name}/{executionId}/{taskRunId}\n- handle(PluginEndpointContext ctx); body is a parsed JSON object (Map),\n  response may name a file (Content-Disposition, sanitized)\n- ScopedStorage confines every URI to the execution storage prefix;\n  logs use the ACL finder; outputs read off the ACL-loaded execution\n- dispatch authorizes the execution (ACL findById + namespace) before\n  resolving the plugin, so an unauthorized caller learns nothing about it\n\n* fix(plugins): address review on scoped plugin endpoints\n\n- read outputs through TaskOutputService (TaskRun.getOutputs() is removed in 2.0)\n- address endpoints by plugin class ({cls}) resolved via RegisteredPlugin.hasClass,\n  which is what the calling task UI holds; endpoints stay plugin-scoped\n- make JSON-only explicit: @Consumes(application/json) + @Body Map<String,Object>\n- ScopedStorage rejects any non-kestra:// URI\n- make the feature toggleable with kestra.plugins.endpoint.enabled (controller not\n  loaded when disabled) and expose it to the UI via /configs\n- make the request-body cap configurable (kestra.plugins.endpoint.max-body-size)\n- rename TaskRunLogs/TaskRunOutputs to ...Fetcher, drop a dead null check\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nKwiatkowski <nkwiatkowski@kestra.io>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw5KPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJrMQAJRypvsLdWurrXIWhNqYyz/+\nPsD13OihBr6Sa4dn6La7a0dx8RDXgGv0E6HXpo8caU3ZWTikDhmeUFpIjV6zIp9U\nJnxxQAnL/pegdZubKNHbfGS3GTxBu9nzqjSwXWIcdSYpUOKlJ6ORaEfdXuhurd+F\n6uxT7kFU7YeuksyL/yujVtzNsPmuw3Gc3XL3BxJGivi7JsBPvdj5yjVoQConH6Hw\nhGkNYDKDgOtN5eJ+ZteSwWhRmiaDjWavP8/EYx79TPU5yyNPbM+Cm7T+lo+pKUBR\nQ5orS4ZOc9ZvtMb7Cv4f6m7Zhwjhk/w6SXm9ME0DOytpZMVvr7Wqvus2PTS06BPJ\nS98tjsKamaBtffauN8CWg3z8sz+hwlDE/TcaQN7Z+CsNVDBBz6lnhWiqIloMneE7\nFvQZ5kdq/3GAEdyZbZ9rR2b15KShJpzn+cRL+0h+b0uqfnEZTQrv+GgEHYkMttDI\n19ZbLDvrwJIGMrh/6uO3ibi0U2bxLgpqiZ+aGMMj+5Q4RA6CLCI+YxXGAFHi7Tpu\njHKXTJBQoirQrBrrf09KdwAPaQxGE0cprmQfgfEpqaX/eSTdCpImnDaxyQnuaAbE\nw3Aoy/5v7duMF6zOnUE+j6KI4zuo2qgdm/PFIq8mq716fBVBcDYaBc/nWVAkIq++\n42a4ZW+CVJ0ktkVhKiLk\n=DogK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T12:05:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.gi