c310b91b798d380c8"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564","sha":"8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564"}],"sha":"62249c45db594bd55fc7ba60b51a3c7b574fc06c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/62249c45db594bd55fc7ba60b51a3c7b574fc06c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:21:16Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(payment-methods): release the auto-select guards when the order loses its payment source\n\nThe auto-select of a single payment method is guarded twice — `loadingResourceRef`\nand `paymentSourceCreated` — so it selects the method, and creates its payment\nsource, once per mount. Neither guard is ever released. The API drops\n`payment_source` whenever the order totals move, and applying a coupon does exactly\nthat, so the guards outlive the thing they were set for and the step dies where it\nstands: no method selected, no gateway form, and not one further request.\n\nThat last part is how it reads in a trace, and it is worth knowing: the requests the\ngateway had in flight sit there with no status and no headers, and nothing follows\nthem. A latched guard makes no noise, because it never retries.\n\nRelease them on the transition that invalidates them — the order going from having a\npayment source to explicitly having none. Keying on the transition, rather than on\n\"there is none right now\", keeps them holding through the window in which the first\npayment source is still being created. And only an explicit `null` counts: an order\nread without the include carries `undefined`, which says nothing about whether a\npayment source exists, and treating the two alike created a second payment source\nover the first while the shopper was still on the form.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fdf79522c43bd161a625c58248ea385921d8b06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/4fdf79522c43bd161a625c58248ea385921d8b06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDhkNGNlNzZhNGJjNWIwYjY3YjQwMWFhNWQyMzY2YThiOGVmMmM1NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb","sha":"c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb"}],"sha":"8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/8d4ce76a4bc5b0b67b401aa5d2366a8b8ef2c564"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:20:21Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(shipments): do not vouch for a revision that dropped our shipping method\n\n`setShippingMethod` stamps the order revision it reads back, so the revalidation\neffect does not refetch shipments for our own update — the hook has already done\nit. Another write can land inside that window, though, and the coupon is the one\nthat matters: the API clears `shipment.shipping_method` while it recalculates the\ntotals. The revision we then read is one the shipments in hand do not reflect, and\nstamping it tells the effect they are in step with an order they contradict.\n\nNothing refetched them again. The step kept a shipping method the order no longer\nhad, `Continue to payment` stayed disabled, and the trace showed no further request\nafter the coupon at all — a deadlock, not a slow load. It reached the checkout as\n`payments-checkoutcom` failing to find the card fields, three steps away from here.\n\nStamp only when the order we read still carries the method we wrote. When it does\nnot, or when the order is not detailed enough to say, let the effect refetch: one\nextra round trip is worth much less than a checkout that cannot be completed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb11be179843bbb14f7a4a9f844ead82fc4fdd95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/bb11be179843bbb14f7a4a9f844ead82fc4fdd95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGM0NjlhNzM0OGQwYjc3YmRjMGMxZTdjNzM4MjFkYzI5OTRjYmFkY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7","sha":"3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7"}],"sha":"c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/c469a7348d0b77bdc0c1e7c73821dc2994cbadcb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:08:16Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(adyen): re-arm the mounted flag so Strict Mode still gets a Drop-in\n\nThe flag guarding the mount was set once, at declaration, and only ever\ncleared. Strict Mode mounts, tears down and mounts again, so the teardown left\nit false for good and the guard then refused every mount: no Drop-in at all,\nand the shopper had nothing to pay with.\n\nSet it on the way into the effect, the way the teardown clears it on the way\nout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2159f532de4b2e993a8d381abf5be3a14f893dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/d2159f532de4b2e993a8d381abf5be3a14f893dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDNiMTdhYjc4M2Y4M2ZhMzgxM2ZiZGM3ODAxNmJjZDZjYTk4ZWI1Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5","sha":"4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5"}],"sha":"3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/3b17ab783f83fa3813fbdc78016bcd6ca98eb5c7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:26:20Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(adyen): do not mount the Drop-in after the component has gone\n\nBuilding the Drop-in is async, and the payment step re-renders while it is in\nflight — applying or removing a coupon does it. The container goes with the\ncomponent, so the mount that follows throws out of Adyen, unhandled:\n\"Component could not mount. Root node was not found.\". The shopper is left on\na payment step that never comes back.\n\nCheck on the way out of the await, not only on the way in, and bail. A\nremounted component initializes a fresh Drop-in as it always did.\n\nMeasured on `payments-adyen-givex:106`: the unhandled rejection goes from two\noccurrences to none. That test still fails, further along and for another\nreason — after the coupon is removed the Drop-in no longer offers Givex.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea68f9547a52e70632c2a7410ccc8c319fece2a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/ea68f9547a52e70632c2a7410ccc8c319fece2a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDRjYjNhMmQwNmE0NTNkODAxYjdlYjg4NjE0OWE0OTJiZmNlOGFiZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29","sha":"8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29"}],"sha":"4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/4cb3a2d06a453d801b7eb886149a492bfce8abd5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:10:52Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(place-order): let a partial payment reach the automatic place attempt\n\nThe automatic place for an authorized Adyen payment was capped at one attempt\nper order per page load, because `handleClick` flips `status` and re-runs the\neffect. A partial payment reaches that effect twice, though — once per leg —\nand the gift card leg spent the single attempt the order was allowed. By the\ntime the card covered the remainder and the order finally read `authorized`,\nnothing was left to place it: the shopper sat on a payment step that had taken\ntheir money.\n\nKey the marker on the order state rather than the order alone, so a genuine\ntransition — partially authorized to authorized — gets its own attempt while\nrepeating the same state still cannot loop.\n\n`payments-adyen-givex` goes from four failures to one, and that one is the\nNext dev-tools overlay swallowing a click.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e8d5ca44b321d4be99d184c1444991362971e11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/2e8d5ca44b321d4be99d184c1444991362971e11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDhhYTEzZTVjM2FiODlhYmY3ZTgyMmUzM2VkNDMyMzM3MzYxOGNjMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d","sha":"a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d"}],"sha":"8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/8aa13e5c3ab89abf7e822e33ed4323373618cc29"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T09:28:41Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(place-order): do not place a partial payment on the gift card leg\n\nThe previous commit let the guard stand down as soon as the gateway validated\nan attempt, on the grounds that a validated attempt means the remainder has\nbeen covered. On a partial payment it does not: the gift card leg validates\ntoo — it did authorize the gift card — so the order was placed before the\nshopper had entered the card at all. Measured on the givex flow: by the time\nthe card was submitted the order already read `placed` / `authorized`, and\nevery write to its payment source came back 401.\n\nSo ask the gateway what is still outstanding. Adyen''s partial-payment order\ncarries the remaining amount; anything without one has no remainder to speak\nof, so a validated attempt covers it by definition.\n\nThis leaves `payments-adyen-givex` where it was before that commit — the four\npartial-payment tests still fail — but an order is never placed with money\nstill owed on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f11073a7446e10731c9e27e51af66c3122b5e7a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/f11073a7446e10731c9e27e51af66c3122b5e7a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGE5MTExOWI4MjU4NDNiZjI2MjZjZTQ2NDI1NmIwOGI1MGRhNjgzMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948","sha":"21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948"}],"sha":"a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a91119b825843bf2626ce464256b08b50da6831d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:54:07Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(payment-methods): stop swallowing a 401 on a payment source write\n\nA 401 here has one benign reading: the order was placed or approved while the\nrequest was in flight, so the token can no longer write to it and the checkout\nis over regardless. The branch stayed quiet for that — and, because it treated\nan unreadable order as the same thing, for everything else too.\n\nEverything else is a write that did not happen. The API refuses to update an\nAdyen payment source on the second leg of a partial payment: the card details\nnever reach the payment source, the order records the gift card as the payment\nmethod, and nothing anywhere says so. Finding that took instrumenting the\ncomponent, because the one signal it produced was a console line.\n\nStay quiet for the benign case only, and when the order cannot be read back\nassume the worst rather than the best.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15410ba9faad265490d58704ca36b6aa6c21371b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/15410ba9faad265490d58704ca36b6aa6c21371b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDIxMjA1ZDIzM2VhN2VlNzVmNjM5MDNiZTliN2YyYWVmZjNlYjg5NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83","sha":"847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83"}],"sha":"21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/21205d233ea7ee75f63903be9b7f2aeff3eb8948"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:43:11Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(place-order): let a partially authorized order be placed once the gateway covers the rest\n\nGivex behaves like a gift card: it can cover part of the total and leave the\norder `partially_authorized`, with the remainder still to be paid by card or\nanother Adyen method. Refusing to place it then is the whole point of the\nguard — the order would go through with that remainder unpaid.\n\nBut the remainder is paid through the gateway widget, and the status the guard\nreads is fetched before the widget runs. With givex the card only authorizes\nas the order is placed, so the order stays `partially_authorized` right up to\nthat moment: the guard rejected the very attempt that pays the rest, and every\nlater attempt read the same status and refused in its turn. Nothing could ever\nplace the order — `payments-adyen-givex` sat waiting for a thank-you page that\nwas never coming.\n\nThe widget validating the attempt is the signal that the remainder has been\ncovered, so the guard now stands down for that attempt only. An attempt with\nno gateway behind it — the click that merely applied the gift card — is\nrefused exactly as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e59a41083a9caa6c013ad3f32d967c3d778246d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/3e59a41083a9caa6c013ad3f32d967c3d778246d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDg0NzQxNGQ3ZDQ5ODQ2YmVhMjYxYmU4ZmU3NDJmZmZlNjk5OWZjODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23","sha":"106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23"}],"sha":"847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/847414d7d49846bea261be8fe742fffe6999fc83"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:34:07Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(order): always fetch the order with its line items\n\nLeaving every include to the components that mount is what broke when the\ncontainers went away, and the fix for it must not be \"the app lists the\nresources it needs\" — no consumer should have to know our resource names to\nget the cart. So the order carries its line items whatever is rendered: it is\nthe one relationship that is not a detail of some component, and by the time a\ncomponent that wants it has mounted, the first fetch is long gone.\n\nEverything past that floor stays with the component that reads it, the way\n`<Shipments>` now asks for `line_items.item`. `include` on `<Order>` remains\nfor an app that reads a relationship off the order with no component of ours\ninvolved, and is expected to go unused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35a3c7a748faacfed22d2ef7253f9c0966684371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/35a3c7a748faacfed22d2ef7253f9c0966684371"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDEwNjM1OWY4ZDg2ODM5MGMwNmNjNmU5ODkxOTg5NDZkNzRlNjRiMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135","sha":"014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135"}],"sha":"106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/106359f8d868390c06cc6e989198946d74e64b23"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:31:09Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(shipments): refetch when the cached shipments predate the order\n\nThe revalidation marker lives on the component, the SWR cache does not. A step\nthat closes and reopens — applying a coupon does exactly that — remounts this\ncomponent with an empty marker, which reads as \"first order I have seen\" and\naccepts whatever the cache holds: shipments fetched before the coupon, still\ncarrying the shipping method the API cleared when the totals moved. The step\ncame back looking settled while the order had no shipping, and the total was\nshort by the shipping amount all the way to place order.\n\nRemember the revision the shipments were fetched at outside the component, so\na remount can tell a warm cache from a fresh one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5aeefd2324084bea9831fe16c529c3bd088ebea1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/5aeefd2324084bea9831fe16c529c3bd088ebea1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDAxNDA0MGMzZjYxMWQ3Njc0YzE1ZmNlZjNmNmQwOGQzYTRlNmIxMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a","sha":"a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a"}],"sha":"014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/014040c3f611d7674c15fcef3f6d08d3a4e6b135"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:07:35Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(addresses): stop the save-to-address-book box killing the step\n\n`saveAddressToCustomerAddressBook` dispatches into the order state, and the\norder context rebuilds it on every state change. Three effects here both\ncalled it and listed it as a dependency, so each one re-ran on its own result.\nHarmless while the flag was false and nothing was dispatched — ticking \"save\nthis address in your account\" started the loop, React gave up with \"Maximum\nupdate depth exceeded\", and the error boundary blanked the customer step. The\ncheckbox went with it, so it looked as if the click had never registered.\n\nCall it through a ref, the way this codebase already does for callbacks that\nfeed the state they read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"544c1d3e5a470ff457ce69df6981467dbb364886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/544c1d3e5a470ff457ce69df6981467dbb364886"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGE2MzRkNGQ4ZDg0MTExMWVjNWQzMmY0ZTU2Yzg4NGViNjlkODNhNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8","sha":"449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8"}],"sha":"a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a634d4d8d841111ec5d32f4e56c884eb69d83a5a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:53:02Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(shipment): do not auto-select the same shipment twice\n\nThe effect re-runs on every new `shipments` identity, and the refetch that\nfollows a selection lands before the API reports the method as set. It then\nselects the same method again — harmless server-side, but a caller passing a\ncallback is told about it twice, which for an analytics caller means a\nduplicate event.\n\nRemember the shipment and method already selected, and forget it as soon as\nthe data catches up, so a method the API clears later (applying a coupon does)\nis still selected again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4eb3e3bfeca9f0e442c7b84330b25219a0f6b811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/4eb3e3bfeca9f0e442c7b84330b25219a0f6b811"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDQ0OWY3M2IzZGJjODY1YmM3Njg2YzJmODUwNGFiMDkxYzRiYjdiZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf","sha":"dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf"}],"sha":"449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/449f73b3dbc865bc7686c2f8504ab091c4bb7be8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:52:15Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(shipments): stop reporting an out-of-stock the data never said\n\nThe stock check reads `line_items.item`, but this component never asked the\norder for it. It arrived by luck from whoever else had mounted —\n`<LineItemsContainer>`, the payment step — and once those stopped wrapping the\nwhole checkout, a shipping step rendered before them saw `item` undefined on\nevery line. Undefined is not \"no stock\": every line failed the check and the\nshipping methods disappeared behind \"an item in your order is no longer\navailable\", on orders with millions of units in the warehouse.\n\nSo: ask for the include like every other component does, and treat a line\nwhose `item` is missing as unknown rather than out of stock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb603d9cece8fb17ee1c4552e92f4b56d5019c26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/cb603d9cece8fb17ee1c4552e92f4b56d5019c26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGRjODA5ZDhlZTg3YjM2ZjJjZjQ3YTYzNTA3MzI0MzY4MzMwNGJkYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6","sha":"59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6"}],"sha":"dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/dc809d8ee87b36f2cf47a635073243683304bdaf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T09:51:20Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:29:44Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"feat(order): let the caller declare the includes up front\n\n`include` is the union of what the mounted components ask for, which was in\ntime while containers wrapped the whole checkout. A standalone component\nmounts with its step, so the first order carries whatever the first component\nto mount asked for — and a relationship the app reads off the order itself,\nrather than through one of our components, is never asked for at all.\n`<Order include>` declares them before the first fetch and re-declares them\nafter the settling round that resets the list.\n\n`includeLoaded` now accumulates like `include` does. It is the half that\ndecides whether the fetch runs: the effect waits for as many loaded flags as\nthere are includes, and two dispatchers in the same effect pass read the same\npre-dispatch snapshot, so replacing the map left the two lists out of step for\ngood and no order was ever fetched.\n\n`line_items` joins ResourceIncluded — already used internally, never spelled\nout in the union.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec54fbd4595ebe9811b5b80c1d9776532b9b7c8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/ec54fbd4595ebe9811b5b80c1d9776532b9b7c8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDU5YTI0NjE3MmE4MjQ4ZTY2NGIyOWE4MDNkMDhlYTYzNzlmN2VmYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/5777ff15931960ddc5a1ef0c310b91b798d380c8","sha":"5777ff15931960ddc5a1ef0c310b91b798d380c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/5777ff15931960ddc5a1ef0c310b91b798d380c8"}],"sha":"59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/59a246172a8248e664b29a803d08ea6379f7efb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55532305?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https:/