ed_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/9209ed123f6993960f34895fff395ca88c92cb72","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDkyMDllZDEyM2Y2OTkzOTYwZjM0ODk1ZmZmMzk1Y2E4OGM5MmNiNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/87a28ace52bc01d470501a74bbdd5f1afc916fc3","sha":"87a28ace52bc01d470501a74bbdd5f1afc916fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/87a28ace52bc01d470501a74bbdd5f1afc916fc3"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe","sha":"c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe"}],"sha":"9209ed123f6993960f34895fff395ca88c92cb72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/9209ed123f6993960f34895fff395ca88c92cb72"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:07:26Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:07:26Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix: stop CommerceLayer handing out a new context value every render\n\nThe provider wrapped its value in an object literal, so every render of\nCommerceLayer gave every consumer a fresh identity. This provider sits at\nthe root of the tree, and consumers put values from it into effect\ndependency arrays — it was the amplifier behind the OrderList refetch loop\nrather than its cause, and it stays a trap for anything else downstream.\n\nThe test needs a fresh child element per render: reusing one element makes\nReact skip rendering the child entirely, and the assertion then measures\nnothing. It fails with the memo removed.\n\nThe five other providers built from object literals are left alone: three\nsit inside .map() callbacks where a per-item memo is awkward and the value\nis a single loop variable, and the remaining two are narrow leaf contexts.\nNone of them wraps the app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"71efe6bb119aef6d9bc8ec7498042dac59298e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/71efe6bb119aef6d9bc8ec7498042dac59298e7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGMyNWM4ZWVkMTA5NWVhN2UwNTI1ODA1NjRlZjAyMjRmYTBjNTQ1ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6","sha":"23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6"}],"sha":"c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/c25c8eed1095ea7e052580564ef0224fa0c545fe"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T09:54:16Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T09:54:16Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"ci: build the packages before linting them\n\nThe first run of this workflow failed, which is the workflow doing its job.\nreact-hooks-components'' lint script ends in `tsc`, and that resolves\n@commercelayer/core-components through its dist/ — absent on a clean\ncheckout, so the package produced 30-odd TS2307 errors and the job stopped\nbefore reaching vitest.\n\nIt passed locally only because a previous build had left dist/ in place.\nnetlify.toml warns about exactly this for the storybook build; the comment\nclaiming no build was needed was right about vitest and wrong about lint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea89c8da61860c2135b321dc9dbda2a18f92a43c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/ea89c8da61860c2135b321dc9dbda2a18f92a43c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDIzOTU2MDE3ZGZkM2M1YTg2OTI0MWQ5M2IzZTBkODM5YmQ4MDIzYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68","sha":"581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68"}],"sha":"23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/23956017dfd3c5a869241d93b3e0d839bd8023c6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T09:51:51Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T09:51:51Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"ci: run the test suites on pull requests\n\nNothing in CI ran the tests. The check that reads \"test / test\" comes from\nmerge-test-env-check.yml, whose `test` job only lists licenses — it takes\nthree seconds and passes regardless of the code. The 1376 tests across the\nthree packages ran only in the local pre-commit hook, so a PR that broke\nthem showed all green.\n\nThis workflow is named unit-tests with a vitest job, rendering as\n\"unit-tests / vitest\", so it cannot be mistaken for the licenses check\nsitting next to it.\n\n`pnpm test` is not reused: the react-components script starts with\n`pnpm audit --prod --audit-level high`, which fails on any newly published\nadvisory and would turn the suite red for reasons unrelated to the change.\nLint and vitest run directly instead. No build step is needed — the vitest\nconfigs alias the sibling workspace packages to their source.\n\nVerified both ways locally: the commands exit 0 on this branch, and exit 1\nwith one of the fixes in this PR reverted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e6f0b642671841a137a1a6dc4cb52df0ffaae92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/3e6f0b642671841a137a1a6dc4cb52df0ffaae92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDU4MWRmOTY1MWIxOWU3Mjg0NzNlMjEzYjE3ZjRjMmQ0NDU4MDRlNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160","sha":"ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160"}],"sha":"581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/581df9651b19e728473e213b17f4c2d445804e68"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T09:51:12Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T09:51:12Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix: keep fieldEvent off the billing form''s DOM element\n\nBillingAddressForm declares fieldEvent in Props but never destructures it,\nso it survives into the rest spread that lands on the <form>:\n\n  React does not recognize the `fieldEvent` prop on a DOM element.\n\nIts twin already does this correctly — ShippingAddressForm.tsx destructures\n`fieldEvent: _fieldEvent = \"change\"` — which is what makes this an omission\nrather than a decision. Neither component reads the prop: it appears nowhere\nelse in src/, so it is accepted, typed, and inert.\n\nFound by scanning for components whose Props extend JSX.IntrinsicElements,\ndeclare non-DOM props, and spread the rest onto a DOM element. Only two\ncandidates survived filtering for real HTML attributes, and the other one\n(AvailabilityTemplate) is a false positive — its extra names live inside a\n`labels` object that is destructured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4018b40e9b1bfced2c6a9b8ff551b11358830d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/b4018b40e9b1bfced2c6a9b8ff551b11358830d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGVmNWUyZDI3NjU1ZTU2MjU1NmZlZTk4NDBlOTJjYmMxNTMwMTQxNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5","sha":"bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5"}],"sha":"ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/ef5e2d27655e562556fee9840e92cbc153014160"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T09:39:51Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T09:39:51Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix: stop OrderList from refetching orders in a loop\n\nOrderList fired a fetch roughly once per API round-trip: the effect that\ncalls getCustomerOrders retriggered itself through two independent routes.\n\n1. useCustomerProviderValue memoized the whole context value with `state`\n   among its deps and spread `...state` into it, so every landed fetch\n   produced a new getCustomerOrders identity — and OrderList has that\n   callback in its effect deps. Split into a stable `actions` memo plus a\n   thin outer memo that joins state and actions; the one callback that\n   read `state.addresses` directly now reads it through a ref.\n\n   The callbacks still change identity when accessToken or customerId\n   change, so a fetch still reruns when the token arrives.\n\n2. defaultSdkSorting was a bare object literal, i.e. a new identity on\n   every render, which refired the effect even with stable callbacks.\n   Memoized on the primitives it derives from.\n\nAlso stop Address from leaking disabledClassName onto the DOM: it was\ndeclared in Props but not destructured, so it survived into the rest\nspread that lands on a <div>. The children-as-function form still\nreceives it through parentProps.\n\nBoth regressions arrived in v5 and are absent from 4.29.7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"409d4beb3a00f7766c5eec65afac38a0ae71dc7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/409d4beb3a00f7766c5eec65afac38a0ae71dc7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGJiYjI5ZTg2MzNhMTE3ZGNjNjRiZmFiNjBjYWVkMmQwNTEyMTFlZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/87a28ace52bc01d470501a74bbdd5f1afc916fc3","sha":"87a28ace52bc01d470501a74bbdd5f1afc916fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/87a28ace52bc01d470501a74bbdd5f1afc916fc3"}],"sha":"bbb29e8633a117dcc64bfab60caed2d051211ee5","url":"ht