:"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #843 from commercelayer/feat/841-shared-state-store\n\nfix: share checkout state across sibling subtrees (#841)","tree":{"sha":"b2a9ac0281d981f26ebe95cc8991d6a985e5d7b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/b2a9ac0281d981f26ebe95cc8991d6a985e5d7b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/ad5fea578176805822cfed3338e6dd08d7780467","verification":{"payload":"tree b2a9ac0281d981f26ebe95cc8991d6a985e5d7b7\nparent 07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986\nparent b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c\nauthor Alessandro Casazza <55532305+acasazza@users.noreply.github.com> 1789401653 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789401653 +0200\n\nMerge pull request #843 from commercelayer/feat/841-shared-state-store\n\nfix: share checkout state across sibling subtrees (#841)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqBo1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFzoQAE8tbN36FD5PkkJwamiiNJHP\nxOtJmCbvATFUuYtycDNDgIykM4yOwf7auG5CQ6L5dU349yZanMhmcjVCScIQ7jRm\ntJouGjEqAYG+4vfaRQW1Y5W4pRysYygeSxoK/yoP42ndDyc64nHfXipQLs34VZGP\naxUHdaJF9WeD+qR9mlgeDmOejSqk0PKjHWlWwrd+q6EKdl1mHrPqDfG1imBypDOz\nlVzuwKirnQroC6vTWnrfwHWddkeFnnkwK+sfhfIKQ8UL+rdO0ngKx39tv2B0zkqv\n4iZDRLNOX3tzleuAymerR5JjhB+WdCke6Etziwe9T7oOs0bBkpd8GJCakkw5dHaC\nDfKxCXY/UovW1B3w9DeyoDCXq1npfLQvJX8TtWJ1sL/xN6lKyjlJeHeHvD+VKx7v\n6pGcIwYr3Q0eNi3lOwpeIjlmNxTxegk58k0SCkFBytaJYy3UEAuCoXkRnzK/esOB\n09ypcwjh3naI8RO55deNjW57AnnrCAEa+a1LrvheAQQQcCusXlcT+Ux4TUi09WsU\nzfd+/0IKYQ4TN3vYjMvuHHW8tTYKFHtWcBE92DHY6N9HgXbFMG6JQbhzjfOtwKt4\nHLxe3/j65zifve9sgx8UjTe4CXIMO7DMzke+PbJrkwg229z0LiS0BLg1WdfkAcx/\neu5NRzpYfM7yvtz9z6CS\n=ffuB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T16:00:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/ad5fea578176805822cfed3338e6dd08d7780467","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGFkNWZlYTU3ODE3NjgwNTgyMmNmZWQzMzM4ZTZkZDA4ZDc3ODA0Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986","sha":"07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c","sha":"b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c"}],"sha":"ad5fea578176805822cfed3338e6dd08d7780467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/ad5fea578176805822cfed3338e6dd08d7780467"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:03:11Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:03:11Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"docs: cover the case the migration guide skipped\n\nThe guide put every example in one subtree, which is the case that already\nworked. The one that sent people to #841 — a save button that is a sibling\nof the forms, a place-order step outside the payment step — was not\nmentioned, so the advice read as complete and broke silently when followed.\n\nIt now says how sibling subtrees find each other, and the two things that\nfollow: state the app owns has to be published by the app, since a UI that\nunmounts a form leaves nobody to publish it, and two deliberate editors on\none order need `scope` to stay apart.\n\nThe hooks page also listed four of the twelve exported hooks and claimed\nReact 18.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2a9ac0281d981f26ebe95cc8991d6a985e5d7b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/b2a9ac0281d981f26ebe95cc8991d6a985e5d7b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGIxYThjYjRhZTI0YjMwNGFjZTVhYjBmMmVhZjdkM2ZmOWRiMzk5M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f","sha":"303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f"}],"sha":"b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/b1a8cb4ae24b304ace5ab0f2eaf7d3ff9db3993c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:50:16Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:50:16Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"feat(containers): warn from every deprecated container, in one voice\n\nEight of the fifteen deprecated containers said nothing at all, including\nthe three that #841 is about. A consumer following the console would migrate\nthe seven that spoke up, end with a clean console, and still have the other\neight in the tree — the silence read as \"nothing left to do\".\n\nThe seven that did warn used three shapes and three sets of brackets:\n`[ShipmentsContainer]`, `<GiftCardContainer>` and a bare `CustomerContainer`,\nsome in an effect, one during render, one behind a module-level flag. They\nall go through one helper now, which also makes a container added without a\nwarning obvious.\n\nThe warning fires per mount rather than once per process. A module-level flag\nmakes tests depend on their order and hides the warning after a hot reload,\nand a container mounted again after a migration is supposed to say so again.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57a6b372a553ed28f9292f02926cab45aea67a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/57a6b372a553ed28f9292f02926cab45aea67a9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDMwM2VkMjNiMDRkZTczNzA5MGQ3MjY1ZjVlMjI2MWY1ZTNhNjA4MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3","sha":"61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3"}],"sha":"303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/303ed23b04de737090d7265f5e2261f5e3a6081f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:45:34Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T12:45:34Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(payment-methods): only ask for the payment includes where they are used\n\nLetting every reader register `payment_method` and `payment_source` meant\n`<Errors>` asked for them too, and that component is mounted on every step.\nThe order was then fetched again during shipping, where nothing needs\npaying — and an order refresh there is exactly the condition under which the\nshipping-method radio reverts to unchecked, a library flake the checkout\nsuite already documents and retries around. It stopped surviving the retry.\n\nThe includes are now requested by the components that render the payment\nsource: `<PaymentMethod>`, which owns the state, and `<PaymentSource>`, which\nis what the order recap mounts on its own.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de8f89eeb57a7bf168e4c767ebd8cb88ff5e6a76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/de8f89eeb57a7bf168e4c767ebd8cb88ff5e6a76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDYxODYxZDM5ZWY2YTY2YjcwMThlY2IyNDNjNTQxOThiMTExZTg5ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081","sha":"841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081"}],"sha":"61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/61861d39ef6a66b7018ecb243c54198b111e89e3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T10:15:06Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T10:15:06Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(payment-methods): keep the payment source in step with the order\n\nThe payment source was derived from the order once, while the method list\nwas still empty. That was enough while the state died with the components\nthat built it: the order recap mounted fresh and derived again. The state\nnow outlives its subscribers on purpose, so the recap kept showing the\nsource as it was before the payment went through — `getCardDetails` returned\nthe \"card\" and \"****\" placeholders instead of the brand and the last four\ndigits, which only arrive when the order is fetched again after being\nplaced.\n\nA fresher representation of the same source now replaces the stored one.\nMatching on the id keeps this to a refresh: it never changes which source is\nselected, so the payment step, where the source is created before the order\nknows about it, is untouched.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"253f4cbab91bed9c8205878033f673e66f821d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/253f4cbab91bed9c8205878033f673e66f821d02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDg0MWQwNDg4YzM4YjY3NmE0MmY4ZmRlODYxNmE2OTQyODIyZGEwODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9","sha":"d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9"}],"sha":"841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/841d0488c38b676a42f8fde8616a6942822da081"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:45:23Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:45:23Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(order): fetch the order again when the include list grows late\n\nThe order was fetched once, while `state.order` was still null, and the\ninclude list was closed from then on. That held while containers wrapped the\nwhole checkout and mounted with it. A standalone component mounts when its\nstep opens, registers its includes then, and the order never carried them —\n`addResourceToInclude` marks a resource loaded in the same breath as\nregistering it, so \"loaded\" meant \"asked for\" and nothing ever noticed the\ngap. `<PaymentMethod>` rendered an empty list at the payment step, and the\norder recap on the last step rendered nothing at all.\n\nThe order is now fetched again whenever the include list grows past what the\ncurrent one was fetched with, coalesced on a 50ms timer. The coalescing is\nthe part that matters: components mount over several ticks and each widens\nthe list, so refetching per growth fires a request per component — enough to\nstall the checkout. It is the same flush `createBatchStore` uses, for the\nsame reason.\n\nWith that in place, a reader can ask for what it needs: `usePaymentMethod`\nregisters `payment_method` and `payment_source` in one call and derives the\nselected method from the order. Reading those off the order is not a request,\nso any instance may do it — which is what the order recap needs, since no\nowner is mounted anywhere near it. `<PaymentSource>` hands the resolved state\ndown to the gateway below it, the way `<PaymentMethod>` already does for its\nown children.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45f03e2df8b05d8763ae9cd1f05ddcdad55e4a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/45f03e2df8b05d8763ae9cd1f05ddcdad55e4a2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGQ1N2JlYjMxNWZhNDY4Mzc4NzkxOTljYzQyZDgxMmUyOGNkNWFjZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad","sha":"46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad"}],"sha":"d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/d57beb315fa46837879199cc42d812e28cd5acf9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:37:58Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:37:58Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(payment-methods): share the payment state with the place-order step\n\nThe deprecation says to use `<PaymentMethod>` standalone, which assumes the\nplace-order button sits inside the payment method subtree. In a stepped\ncheckout it does not: the payment step and the place-order step are\nsiblings, and `PlaceOrderButton` reads `PaymentMethodContext` with no\nfallback at all. Removing the container left it without\n`currentPaymentMethodType`, without `paymentSource` and with a dispatch-less\n`setPaymentSource` — a failure at the money step.\n\nThe state moves into a store shared per order, the same way as the address\nand place-order state. `<PaymentMethod>` still provides the context to its\nown children, so the gateways and payment sources below it are untouched;\nwhat changes is that components outside that subtree now find the state too.\n\n`<PaymentMethod>` owns it and everyone else only reads: a reader must not\nre-register the order includes or refetch the payment methods.\n\nThe spec now clears the shared stores before and after each test. A fetch\nleft in flight by one test resolves into the store once the next has\nstarted, which is a property of state that deliberately outlives its\nsubscribers.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a29fdf71672bdfffb99579fc25b4947365108fc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/a29fdf71672bdfffb99579fc25b4947365108fc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDQ2ZTZiYzAyOWEyMzYxYzNjMmQwYjFjMzk1MDMyMThiMmY2MDdmYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0","sha":"05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0"}],"sha":"46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/46e6bc029a2361c3c2d0b1c39503218b2f607fad"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:23:56Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:23:56Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"docs(adr): record why the shared state is a store and not a provider\n\nIssue #841 asks for a provider per context, and we did not do that. Anyone\nreading the issue in six months needs to find the reasoning, the three\nalternatives that were weighed, and the consequences that cannot be read off\nthe code: entries outliving their subscribers, state owned by the\napplication having to be published by the application, and the two\ninvariants the stores rely on.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dba9a4786ecf68188657f33e401d201f607d50cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/dba9a4786ecf68188657f33e401d201f607d50cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDA1YTFkYWJiM2Q3YTM4ZjQ1YWVkNjJjOWQ4YjdjNTg1Yzc2YjZjZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc","sha":"fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc"}],"sha":"05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/05a1dabb3d7a38f45aed62c9d8b7c585c76b6cd0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T17:05:18Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T17:05:18Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(place-order): share the place-order state across the payment step\n\n`<PlaceOrderButton>` has a standalone fallback but never provided\n`PlaceOrderContext`, so the six components that read it — `PaymentMethod`,\n`PaymentMethodRadioButton`, `PaymentGateway` and the Adyen, Stripe and\nCheckout.com payment sources — were left on the default context once the\ncontainer was dropped. The status readers degraded quietly to \"standby\";\nAdyen was the sharp edge, with no `setPlaceOrder` and no button ref, so its\nprogrammatic place was simply dead.\n\nThe state moves into a store shared per order. `useSharedReducer` keeps the\nexisting reducer and every existing action untouched and only changes where\nthe state is held, so nothing about placing an order had to be rewritten.\n\nThe button ref lives there too. Freezing a snapshot is shallow, so the ref\nobject stays mutable and keeps its identity — which is all the gateways need.\n\nOne instance owns the state and the rest only read it. The owner registers\nthe order includes, evaluates whether placing is permitted and looks up the\norganization config; the payment components would otherwise each redo the\ncontainer''s work, and six token decodes of a fake token is what surfaced it.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c4c2391289c1a92075d4fbf912e3a87d7d9fddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/2c4c2391289c1a92075d4fbf912e3a87d7d9fddd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGZjZDBkZmExMmFlOWJkYjg0NGEyZDQ2NDVhZTgwMDQ0YzZhNWUzZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921","sha":"a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921"}],"sha":"fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/fcd0dfa12ae9bdb844a2d4645ae80044c6a5e3fc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:12:53Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:12:53Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(addresses): wire the address-book components to the shared state too\n\n`<BillingAddress>`, `<ShippingAddress>` and `<Address>` sit outside the forms\nin the customer flow, so without a container they read the empty default\ncontext: `setCloneAddress` was a no-op and the selection flags were never\nthere. Picking a saved address recorded nothing and the save button stayed\ndisabled for good — the same gap as the save button, in three more places.\n\nThey now go through `useAddressStateContext`, which hands back the container''s\ncontext when there is one and the shared state when there is not. Components\nthat only read publish no flags, so they never overwrite what the forms set.\n\nFound by running the mfe-checkout wallet suite against this branch, not by\nreading: the click timed out on a button that could never become enabled.\n\nThe address specs provided a hand-made `AddressContext` without\n`saveAddresses`, which now reads as standalone; they declare it, since a\nprovided context means a container is above.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1a4462d015469abd674a73c6cd0bdc947e8fd22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/c1a4462d015469abd674a73c6cd0bdc947e8fd22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGE3NmM1MDRjYjg3NzU2ZTJlM2M1YzE5NmVkYzVmZDU2NTJkYjM5MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48","sha":"02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48"}],"sha":"a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/a76c504cb87756e2e3c5c196edc5fd5652db3921"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:12:03Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:12:03Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(addresses): let the save button reach the forms it saves\n\n`<SaveAddressesButton>` is a sibling of the two address forms — it has to be,\nsince it saves both — and in standalone mode it read an `AddressContext` that\nnobody had provided. `saveAddresses` was `undefined` there, so none of the\ncases in `handleClick` matched: the button did nothing, with no error and no\nwarning. This is the failure #841 opens with.\n\nThe standalone address state now lives in the shared store behind\n`useAddressForm`, keyed by access token and order, so the forms and the button\nconverge on one state wherever they sit in the tree.\n`useStandaloneAddress` keeps its shape and goes on providing\n`AddressesContext` to each form''s own children, so the components reading that\ncontext are untouched.\n\nTwo more things the button could not do before. It now validates: the forms\nregister their validator through the shared state, because the form contexts\nthey provide only reach their own children and a sibling button never saw\n`errorMode` or `validate` at all. And the non-null assertion on `errors`\nis gone — with the default context that expression threw.\n\nWithout an order the state is keyed by access token alone, so the customer\naddress book, where a form and its save button are siblings too and no order\nexists, shares state the same way.\n\nCloses #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef9be2af724c4479fa24136698fbf87f7530b919","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/ef9be2af724c4479fa24136698fbf87f7530b919"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDAyZDlkMTAwZjljMjgzNWJlMDNmMWI5OGU3OTQzNGViMDI1NWVlNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3","sha":"f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3"}],"sha":"02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/02d9d100f9c2835be03f1b98e79434eb0255ee48"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:02:08Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:02:08Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"feat(hooks): let the caller own the order in useAddressForm\n\nTwo seams for a caller that already manages the order. `order` hands the\nhook an order it already holds, so it does not fetch a second copy of what\nthe caller has on screen. `updateOrder` hands back the write, so an app\nwhose order lives in its own store applies the change there and the store\nstays the single source of truth.\n\nBoth are needed by react-components, whose `OrderContext` owns the order and\nhas to learn about the address update, but neither is specific to it.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"33415425b07ae3f4a93575e8899c8f33201d11da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/33415425b07ae3f4a93575e8899c8f33201d11da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGYyYjU5MTNmOWM0YzkzZDk3NjgxYzAzZjBiZTg2ODcyYjE0NDYyZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa","sha":"4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa"}],"sha":"f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/f2b5913f9c4c93d97681c03f0be86872b14462f3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:59:40Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:59:40Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"feat(hooks): carry the address flags, clone ids and per-form errors\n\nEverything a component sitting outside the forms needs in order to save them\nnow travels through the shared state: `shipToDifferentAddress`, `isBusiness`\nand `invertAddresses` via `setFlags`, the two clone ids via `setCloneIds`,\nand per-form validation errors via `setResourceErrors`, which replaces one\nform''s errors while leaving the other''s in place.\n\n`saveAddresses` reads all of them from the store and still lets an explicit\nargument win, so a caller that knows better is not forced to publish state\nfirst.\n\nField-level writing stays on the react-components side: the form components\nclean their own prefixed values and hand over the finished address, so the\npublic hook does not inherit a vocabulary — prefixed resources, clone ids\nkeyed by resource name, `save_to_customer_book` — that belongs to a reducer\nwe intend to delete.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"290bc7f6aec5fac62defe688423e5fd80881d531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/290bc7f6aec5fac62defe688423e5fd80881d531"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDRkOTNlOWUwNmI1M2ZjZTM4ZmRhYWU2NDk5NWZlYjM4MDUzZDUxZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd","sha":"f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd"}],"sha":"4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/4d93e9e06b53fce38fdaae64995feb38053d51fa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:53:58Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:53:58Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"fix(core): close the gaps between saveOrderAddresses and the reducer\n\n`saveOrderAddresses` was ported from the address reducer in react-components\nbut lost two behaviours on the way, and the reducer cannot be retired until\nthey are back.\n\n`invertAddresses` had no equivalent at all: the reducer builds the order\naround the shipping address and treats billing as the optional second one,\nsetting `_billing_address_same_as_shipping`. Customers use it. The branch is\nported as it stands, including two asymmetries against the normal flow that\nare long-standing behaviour rather than oversights — it updates an existing\naddress without checking that its reference is null, and it does not ask for\na refresh. The one thing that does change is that the input objects are no\nlonger mutated while metadata keys are collected.\n\nThe `do_not_ship` guard was also missing: an order whose every line item\nships nothing has no shipping address to keep in step with the billing one,\nso `_shipping_address_same_as_billing` must stay off. An order with no line\nitems loaded reads as \"not digital-only\", as before.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"797a711a5717f7f51f0a3f93b1eb0c3c307e6544","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/797a711a5717f7f51f0a3f93b1eb0c3c307e6544"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGY4MjA4ZTU1YmY5NTc0NmE2ODU5MDQ3ZThiZGI3YzRhOWI1Yjc3YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7","sha":"d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7"}],"sha":"f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/f8208e55bf95746a6859047e8bdb7c4a9b5b77bd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:20:31Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:20:31Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"feat(hooks): back useAddressForm with shared state, errors and validators\n\nThe hook held its form values in `useState`, so two instances working on the\nsame order saw independent values. That made it unusable for the case it\nexists to serve: the button that saves the addresses is a sibling of the\nforms — it has to be, since it saves both — and would have posted its own\nempty bag while the customer''s input sat in the forms'' instances.\n\nThe values, the saving flag, the validation errors and the validators now\nlive in a module-level store keyed by access token and order id, so every\ninstance converges wherever it sits in the tree. `scope` opts out for the\nrare case of two deliberate editors on one order, and an instance with no\norder id keeps private state rather than dropping what is typed.\n\nTwo additions the sibling button needs: `errors` / `setErrors`, and\n`registerValidator` / `validateAddresses`, so a component outside the forms\ncan validate them before saving instead of saving unvalidated input.\n\nThe SWR key also moves to `[\"order\", \"retrieve\", accessToken, orderId]`,\nmatching `useOrder`. It used to be `order-${orderId}`, which held a second\ncache entry for the same order that never invalidated with the first. The\nhook has no consumers yet, so nothing depended on the old key.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31d0cada8089907c0415ecb0d671ef9ccb119958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/31d0cada8089907c0415ecb0d671ef9ccb119958"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKGQzZWY1ZWNmZmFhMWM3Yzk4ZjJiOTllNjI1ZThhNzRlZGQ0NzkzYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2","sha":"309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2"}],"sha":"d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/d3ef5ecffaa1c7c98f2b99e625e8a74edd4793a7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:15:11Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T10:15:11Z","email":"acasazza@commercelayer.io","name":"Alessandro Casazza"},"message":"feat(core): add a module-level shared state store factory\n\nContext only flows down, so components sitting in sibling subtrees cannot\nshare state through it. `createBatchStore` already solves the fetch half of\nthat problem; this factory solves the other half, the state that never\nreaches the API: form values being typed, the payment method currently\nselected, a place-order status, validation errors.\n\nTwo deliberate differences from `createBatchStore`: no debounce, because UI\nstate must propagate on the tick it changes; and entries outlive their\nsubscribers, because a stepped checkout unmounts whole subtrees between\nsteps and half-typed values must survive the round trip. Entries are keyed\nby access token and order id, so a new session never reads an old one.\n\nRefs #841\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7bf3debdcc671dfe92aec80db100f6574ea0b18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/trees/b7bf3debdcc671dfe92aec80db100f6574ea0b18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/git/commits/309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2","node_id":"C_kwDODH1HQdoAKDMwOWMxZjcyZGY2YTRhMmY0N2U3NjIwYzI1YWU2YTVhYTUwMjVhYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commit/07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986","sha":"07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/07764eb01e5efcdc49c9bcbee0ba97e2aaa04986"}],"sha":"309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/commercelayer/commercelayer-react-components/commits/309c1f72df6a4a2f47e7620c25ae6a5aa5025ab2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55532305?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/acasazza","id":55532305,"login":"acasazza","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NTMyMzA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acasazza/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.g